      "narrative": "Alsym Energy is a Series C climate and energy technology company that has raised approximately $110\u2013111M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy) alongside broader Climate & Energy comparables including public reference points.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $110M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C progression, implying a valuation of $187M. The peer-median method evaluates Alsym against three direct stage and sector comparables, which exhibit a median valuation of $1.0B with a range of $700M to $3.0B, reflecting wide dispersion within the frontier-energy venture market. The peer median is weighted as the primary comparable given specificity of match.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a valuation range of $159M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $594M. The wide range reflects two sources of uncertainty: (1) material heterogeneity within the peer set\u2014KoBold Metals trades at 4.3x the floor set by Amogy\u2014and (2) sparse public market anchors in frontier energy technology. The $594M median represents a reasonable mid-point, though validation of technology differentiation and path to commercialization would be required to narrow this range meaningfully.",
