      "narrative": "Ursa Space Systems is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised approximately $67M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private-market equivalents in the same sector and stage band, including Sierra Space, Impulse Space, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $67M raised proxy, implying a valuation of $114M. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to lack of disclosed revenue. The wide dispersion in private peer valuations\u2014from $1.15B (floor) to $8.0B (Sierra Space)\u2014reflects material heterogeneity in stage, commercial traction, and capital intensity within frontier aerospace.\n\nThe two applicable methods suggest a valuation range of $97M to $2.3B, with a median estimate of $1.1B. The gap between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects Ursa's early funding history relative to sector peer valuations at comparable development stages. Key uncertainties include current revenue run-rate, customer concentration, technical risk profile, and proximity to meaningful commercial milestones\u2014factors that would materially narrow this range.",
