      "narrative": "AheadComputing is a Seed-stage semiconductor design company founded by Marr, Dechene, Pearce, and Srinivasan, having raised $51.5M to date. The valuation universe comprises 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched, though no narrow same-stage peer set with sufficient density exists for direct comparable valuation.\n\nOf three triangulation methods examined, only stage-progression valuation proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($52M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical Seed-to-next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $129M. The public Semiconductors peer set exhibits a median price-to-sales multiple of 18.9x across ALAB, NVDA, and AMD; however, this method cannot be applied due to the absence of disclosed revenue figures for AheadComputing, as is standard for private companies at this stage.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $109M (low) to $148M (high), with a median point of $129M. This range reflects stage-typical progression assumptions but carries material uncertainty. Key limitations include reliance on a single applicable method, absence of comparable transaction data within the narrow Seed-stage Chips & Semiconductors cohort, and lack of revenue or unit economics to anchor public market multiples. The valuation should be updated upon disclosure of financial metrics or when sufficient comparable financings emerge.",
