      "narrative": "Aurora Innovation is a public-stage autonomous systems company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, founded by Chris Urmson, Sterling Anderson, and Drew Bagnell, having raised $2.0B to date. The sector composition includes eight private peers and zero public comparables, with the most developed private players including Joby Aviation, Archer Aviation, Waymo, Wayve, and Zipline.\n\nPeer-median valuation methodology is not applicable to this analysis. The Drones & Autonomous sector contains only seven same-sector peers total, and filtering by stage, adjacency, or valuation tier yields fewer than the three datapoints required for a defensible median benchmark. Applying an all-sector median would introduce material distortion given the heterogeneity of business models and commercialization timelines within autonomous systems.\n\nWithout sufficient narrow-peer triangulation, this valuation cannot be anchored to a specific quantitative range at this time. A credible analysis would require either: expansion of the comp set through relaxation of filtering criteria (accepting greater heterogeneity), introduction of alternative methods such as discounted cash flow analysis with disclosed Aurora financials, or wait-and-see accumulation of public comparables as peers exit private markets. The primary uncertainty is not sector definition but sample size: the universe of meaningful peers remains too sparse for statistical rigor.",
