      "narrative": "Standard Electron is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Tyler Norwood and Alex Le Roux, having raised approximately $3.2M to date. The comparable universe in Climate & Energy includes eight private peers\u2014among them Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix\u2014plus one public company (LNZA). However, insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables exist to support a peer-median valuation method; the broader peer set lacks the density required for reliable multiples triangulation.\n\nGiven these constraints, stage-progression analysis is the applicable valuation method. Using the $3.2M total raised as a proxy for current embedded value and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $8M. This reflects expected value creation through product development and de-risking ahead of Series A financing.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $7M (low) to $9.2M (high), with a median of $8M. This narrow band reflects reliance on a single methodology rather than convergence across multiple methods. Key uncertainties include the pace of technology validation, competitive positioning within the climate-tech stack, and capital-intensity to next meaningful milestone. The lack of tight peer comparables at Seed stage limits precision; future rounds would benefit from expanded peer set density or explicit fundraising guidance.",
