      "narrative": "Slate Auto is a Series C transportation company founded by Miles Arnone, Will Barker, and Jeff Wilke (former CEO of Worldwide Consumer at Amazon). The company has raised $1.4B to date. The transportation technology peer set comprises eight private companies, including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, ZeroAvia, and Harbinger; no public comparables exist in a sufficiently narrow peer cohort.\n\nThe valuation analysis applies stage-progression methodology, which is applicable given the company's defined Series C stage. Using total capital raised ($1.4B) as a proxy for pre-money value and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C-to-later-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $2.4B. Peer-median analysis was not feasible; while three same-sector peers exist in Transportation, none met minimum thresholds (\u22653 datapoints) within same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier filters. Relying on broader sector medians would introduce unacceptable comparability noise.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $2.0B to $2.7B, with a median point of $2.4B. This range is derived from a single applicable method, which represents a material constraint. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct stage-peer benchmarks and the reliance on capital-raised as a valuation proxy rather than operational or market-based metrics. Investors should validate assumptions around typical step-up multiples within this company's specific funding environment and sector dynamics.",
