      "narrative": "Lux Aeterna is a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Brian Taylor, whose prior roles span SpaceX Starlink, Amazon Project Kuiper, and Loft Orbital. The company has raised $14M to date. The valuation exercise draws on a comp universe of 6 public Space & Aerospace peers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nOnly one method produced a usable output: Stage-Progression anchoring. Using total capital raised ($14M) as a proxy for seed-stage valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A progression yields $35M. This method is applicable given the company's clear staging but does not benefit from triangulation with peer medians or public comparables. Peer-median analysis was inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage private peers in the narrow aerospace space (1 same-stage, 0 adjacent). Public-comp anchoring could not proceed without disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $30M\u2013$40M, centered on $35M. This range carries material uncertainty given reliance on a single method and the absence of comparable transaction data or revenue visibility typical of very-early-stage spacecraft and launch operators. Founder pedigree and capital deployment trajectory warrant close monitoring but do not materially refine this estimate without operational milestones.",
