      "narrative": "Diraq is a Series A quantum computing company founded by Andrew Dzurak that has raised over $100M to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public comparables (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nValuation triangulation relied on a single applicable method: stage-progression analysis. Using the $100M total raised as a valuation proxy, a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement yields an implied valuation of $200M. Peer-median analysis was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow quantum computing universe\u2014while 8 private quantum firms exist, none met filtering criteria for meaningful peer clustering. A cross-sector median approach was rejected to avoid diluting sector-specific signals.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $170M to $230M, with a median estimate of $200M. Key uncertainties include the applicability of standard stage-progression multiples in the early-stage quantum sector, where funding velocity and capital intensity may diverge from typical venture patterns. The sparse comparable set limits confidence in peer-based anchoring and leaves technology differentiation, IP position, and near-term commercialization milestones as material variables not captured in quantitative analysis.",
