      "narrative": "Epirus is a Series D defense and security technology company that has raised over $550M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of ten comparable companies\u2014two public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and eight private firms\u2014all operating in the Defense & Security sector at similar stages.\n\nTwo quantitative methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to the last post-money valuation of $1.4B, applies a typical 1.5x step-up multiplier for Series D advancement, implying $2.0B. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Saronic ($9.2B), Quantum-Systems ($8.0B), Chaos Industries ($4.5B), True Anomaly ($2.2B), and Onebrief ($2.1B)\u2014yields a median valuation of $4.5B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $9.2B.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $1.7B (low) to $5.2B (high), with a median of $3.3B. The wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity within the peer cohort; notably, the three largest comparables (Saronic, Quantum-Systems, Chaos) trade at significant premiums to smaller peers. Key uncertainties include whether Epirus's market position and growth profile align with upper-quartile peers or mid-range comparables, and the degree to which public market multiples in defense tech remain applicable to private valuations in the current environment.",
