      "narrative": "Saronic is a Series D-stage defense and security company founded by Dino Mavrookas, Rob Lehman, Vibhav Altekar, and Doug Lambert, currently valued at $9.25B following $2.6B+ in cumulative fundraising. The valuation assessment draws from a comp universe of 10 companies\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014including same-stage peers Quantum-Systems ($8.0B), Chaos Industries ($4.5B), True Anomaly ($2.2B), Onebrief ($2.1B), and Anduril Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $4.0B last post-money valuation and applying a typical Series D-to-next-stage multiplier of 1.5x, implies a valuation of $6.0B. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median of $3.4B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $8.0B. These approaches produced a low of $2.8B, median of $4.7B, and high of $6.9B.\n\nThe current $9.25B valuation sits substantially above both methods' implied ranges. Key uncertainties include revenue growth trajectory relative to peers, competitive positioning within the crowded defense-tech private market, and whether Series D momentum justifies the premium. The gap between triangulated guidance ($4.7B median) and stated valuation warrants scrutiny of non-comparable value drivers or market conditions specific to this round.",
