      "narrative": "Firefly Aerospace is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Tom Markusic with a current valuation of approximately $2.9B following its $868M IPO. The valuation analysis relies on a comparable universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage peers: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach given the target's public status. The median valuation across the four comparables is $23.8B, with a range spanning $840M at the low end (Astroscale) to $1.6T at the high end (SpaceX). This wide dispersion reflects material differences in technology maturity, addressable market, and revenue generation across the peer set. Public-comp anchoring using P/S multiples (median 24.4x across 6 Space & Aerospace tickers) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue data.\n\nThe triangulation analysis supports a valuation range of $20.2B to $27.3B, centered on $23.8B. This median implies a material uplift from Firefly's current $2.9B valuation. The primary uncertainty stems from peer heterogeneity: SpaceX's $1.6T valuation significantly influences the upper bound, while smaller players like Astroscale anchor the lower end. Without granular revenue or contract pipeline data for Firefly, reliance on peer medians introduces execution risk into any valuation assertion.",
