      "narrative": "Palantir is a public-stage AI & Software company with a current market capitalization of $312.5B, having raised $3B+ before its IPO. The valuation analysis is constrained by a limited peer universe: only one public comparable (PLTR itself) and eight identified private peers in the AI & Software sector, including Figure AI, Scale AI, Reflection AI, Applied Intuition, and Skild AI. This composition reflects the highly specialized nature of frontier-tech software infrastructure.\n\nThe peer-median approach is not applicable in this instance. While 11 same-sector peers exist across AI & Software, applying narrow stage-matching or valuation-tier filters yields fewer than three datapoints in any sub-category, rendering a statistically meaningful median calculation impossible. An all-sector median would introduce material confounding factors and obscure rather than illuminate valuation drivers specific to Palantir's market position and business model.\n\nThe lack of sufficient narrow-set comparables underscores a fundamental challenge in valuing frontier-tech infrastructure at scale: few public or private companies operate at Palantir's combination of stage, capitalization, and market tier. Without adequate triangulation via peer multiples, alternative methods\u2014including discounted cash flow analysis with explicit revenue and growth assumptions, or precedent transaction analysis within the data systems category\u2014would be required to establish a defensible valuation range. The current $312.5B market cap thus stands as an observed price, pending additional methodological support.",
