      "narrative": "DIRAC is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Fil Aronshtein that has raised $5M+. The valuation universe consists of nine private peers and one public comparable in the robotics and manufacturing sector, including companies such as Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nDue to insufficient narrow-set peer data, only the stage-progression method is applicable. This approach uses the $5M total raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression, yielding an implied valuation of $12M. The peer-median method cannot be reliably applied\u2014while 11 same-sector peers exist in the broader robotics and manufacturing universe, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier companies yielded fewer than three datapoints, making median-based triangulation statistically unreliable.\n\nThe single-method analysis supports a valuation range of $11M to $14M, with a median of $12M. Key uncertainties include the limited peer set available at seed stage within this subsector and the reliance on a 2.5x multiplier that may not reflect DIRAC's specific market position or growth trajectory. Additional transparency on revenue, customer traction, or proprietary IP would strengthen the valuation. The range should be considered indicative pending fuller market data or comparable transactions.",
