      "narrative": "Formic, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Saman Farid and Misa Ilkhechi, has raised $56M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (277810.KQ), all operating in robotics and manufacturing at Series A through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy base and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement, implies a $112M valuation. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector comparables\u2014Humanoid ($1.4B Series A), Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), and Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B)\u2014yields a median of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation spans $95M to $1.9B, with a median of $881M. The stage-progression method indicates lower bound territory, while peer comparables suggest substantially higher values reflecting the sector's capital intensity and growth multiples. Key uncertainties include the significant stage heterogeneity within the peer set and whether early-stage fundamentals at Formic (product maturity, revenue traction, customer pipeline) justify median or upper-quartile peer valuations. A detailed operational and market assessment is required to narrow this wide range.",
