      "narrative": "Rangeview is a Seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Cameron Schiller and Aeden Gasser-Brennan. The company has raised $5M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comp universe of 9 private robotics and manufacturing firms and 1 public peer, though a narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier limited direct comparable application.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable triangulation approach. Using the $5M total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $12M. This method is well-suited to early-stage companies where funding history provides a concrete anchor. Peer-median analysis was not applicable; while 11 robotics and manufacturing peers exist in the broader dataset, fewer than three companies satisfied simultaneous filters for stage, stage-adjacency, and valuation tier, making a narrow peer median unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $11M to $14M, centered at $12M. This range reflects the stage-progression methodology with conservative ($10.6M) and optimistic ($14.4M) bounds. Key uncertainties include the strength of Rangeview's differentiation relative to the broader peer set\u2014particularly firms like Walden Robotics, Divergent, and Exotec\u2014and forward capital efficiency. Validation against a larger same-stage comparable set would improve confidence in the median estimate.",
