      "narrative": "Mammoth Biosciences, a Series D biotech company founded by Jennifer Doudna and others, has raised $465M+ to date. Valuation is assessed against a universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B, Series C), Chai Discovery ($3.8B, Series C), and New Limit ($3.1B, Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier to the $465M total raised proxy, implying $698M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a $3.8B median, with a range of $3.1B\u2013$10.3B. Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales (8.1x median across biotech tickers) cannot be applied due to the absence of target revenue disclosure, standard for private companies.\n\nTriangulated valuation range: $593M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.2B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage-relative positioning and peer selection. Stage-progression offers a floor grounded in capital deployed; peer median reflects actual market pricing but is sensitive to comparability assumptions and the high valuation outlier (Colossal at $10.3B). Reconciling this range requires clarity on Mammoth's clinical stage, IP defensibility, and market size relative to peers.",
