      "narrative": "Xcimer Energy is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Conner Galloway and Alexander Valys that has raised over $100M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy, representing same-sector players across seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, anchoring to $100M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yields $200M. Peer-median valuation across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014produces a median of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B reflecting stage dispersion.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $170M to $929M, with a median of $504M. The $734M spread between methods reflects material uncertainty around stage-appropriate multiples and peer selection bias toward both early-stage and substantially further-progressed companies. Key unknowns include capital efficiency relative to peers, technology risk, and regulatory pathway clarity specific to Xcimer's approach within the broader nuclear sector.",
