      "narrative": "Base Power, founded by Zach Dell and Justin Lopas, is a Series C\u2013stage climate and energy company that has raised over $1.0B to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage private companies\u2014KoBold Metals ($3.0B), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B), and Amogy ($700M)\u2014alongside one public comparable (LNZA) and eight additional private benchmarks in the Climate & Energy sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method, using the $1.0B total raised as a proxy base value and applying a typical 1.7x Series C step-up multiplier, yields $1.7B. The peer-median approach across the three direct comparables produces $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These methods triangulate to a valuation range of $850M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median implied value of $1.4B.\n\nThe $1.4B median reflects reasonable positioning within the peer cohort, though material uncertainty remains. The wide spread across peer valuations ($700M\u2013$3.0B) and Base Power's limited disclosed financial metrics constrain precision. Key variables affecting valuation include technology maturity, capital efficiency, customer traction, and competitive positioning within the energy transition market.",
