      "narrative": "Claros, a seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Daniel Kultran and Grant Verstandig, has raised $30M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a sector peer set comprising one public company (LNZA) and eight private firms including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, the peer-median method proved inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow climate and energy universe; no cohort of three or more peers satisfied the filtering criteria.\n\nStage-progression analysis, applied to the $30M raised proxy as a base value, yielded a $75M post-money valuation using a 2.5x multiplier typical for seed-to-next-stage advancement in this sector. This single applicable method forms the foundation of the triangulation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $64M to $86M, centered on a $75M median. This range reflects \u00b115% variation around the stage-progression result. Key uncertainties include the limited applicability of peer comparables\u2014a persistent constraint in frontier-climate investing where stage-appropriate, sector-specific public and private data remain sparse\u2014and the appropriateness of the 2.5x multiplier to Claros' specific capital intensity and go-to-market timeline. Additional diligence on burn rate and runway would strengthen confidence in this range.",
