      "narrative": "Etched is a Series E-stage semiconductor chip company that has raised $800M to date against a current post-money valuation of $5.0B. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of eight private companies in the chips and semiconductors sector at the same or adjacent funding stages, anchored by comparables including SambaNova Systems ($11.0B, Series F), Ayar Labs ($3.8B, Series E), Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D), and Nearfield Instruments ($1.6B, Series D). Public semiconductor benchmarks (NVDA, AMD, ALAB) are available but uninformative for this target absent revenue disclosure.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.4x multiplier to the $5.0B last post-money valuation, implying $7.0B. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector comparables yields a median of $3.2B, with a range spanning $1.6B to $11.0B. The peer set reflects meaningful dispersion\u2014a 6.9x spread between floor and ceiling\u2014reflecting variation in technology differentiation and stage maturity within the semiconductor frontier-tech landscape.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a valuation range of $2.7B to $8.0B with a median of $5.1B. The current $5.0B post-money sits near the midpoint, suggesting fair-value alignment. Key uncertainties include revenue traction (undisclosed), technology defensibility relative to higher-valued peers like SambaNova, and nearterm fundraising conditions in the sector.",
