      "narrative": "Distributed Spectrum is a Seed-stage company in Defense & Security founded by Alex Wulff, Ben Harpe, and Isaac Struhl. The company has raised $25M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression methodology uses the $25M total raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series transitions, implying a valuation of $62M. Peer-Median analysis examines three same-sector comparables (UFORCE at Seed valued at $1.0B; Singularity at Series A valued at $400M; NODA AI at Series A valued at $125M), yielding a median of $400M. The peer range spans $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods implies a valuation range of $53M to $460M, with a median of $231M. The substantial variance between stage-based and peer-based approaches reflects material uncertainty around where Distributed Spectrum sits relative to its competitive set in terms of execution, market traction, and technology maturity. Stage-progression alone understates valuation given defense-tech peer benchmarks; peer comparison introduces wide dispersion due to heterogeneous funding rounds and valuations across the cohort.",
