      "narrative": "Bedrock Energy is a Series A climate and energy company founded by Joselyn Lai, Silviu Livescu, and Joel Wishkovsky. The target operates within a competitive frontier sector; our comp universe includes one public company (Linnea Energy, LNZA) and eight private peers spanning similar technology and infrastructure plays, including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, a sufficiently narrow cohort of same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting strict valuation tier criteria was not available to support peer-median analysis.\n\nValuation triangulation relied on stage-progression methodology applied to Bedrock's $15M+ total raised as a base proxy. Using a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A advancement yields an implied valuation of $30M. This single-method approach establishes the central point of our analysis. Peer-median methods were deemed not applicable due to insufficient data density in the narrow Climate & Energy Series A slice; broader sectoral comparisons risked introducing bias.\n\nOur analysis supports a valuation range of $26M to $34M, with a median point of $30M. Key uncertainties include the lack of direct same-stage comparables to validate the step-up multiplier, execution risk on capital deployment given early-stage positioning, and sector-specific regulatory and commodity price exposure. A widened comp set or operational milestones post-Series A would strengthen conviction in this range.",
