      "narrative": "Helsing, a Series E defense and security company founded by Gundbert Scherf, Niklas K\u00f6hler, and Torsten Reil, is currently valued at $18.0B post-money following $1.6B+ in total capital raised. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 firms\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private\u2014spanning the same sector and stage cohort, including Saronic ($9.2B, Series D), Quantum-Systems ($8.0B, Series D), Chaos Industries ($4.5B, Series D), Skydio ($4.4B, Series F), and True Anomaly ($2.2B, Series D).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using a 1.4x multiplier typical for Series E advancement, implies a forward valuation of $25.2B. Peer-median analysis across the 6-firm same-sector, same/adjacent-stage sample yields $4.5B, with a range spanning $2.1B to $9.2B. The disparity between methods reflects Helsing's current positioning at the high end of peer valuations; the peer cohort contains predominantly Series D firms, creating structural comparability constraints.\n\nThe triangulated analysis implies a valuation range of $3.8B (low) to $29.0B (high), with a median of $14.8B. The current $18.0B valuation sits above the median, driven by Helsing's later stage relative to most peers. Key uncertainties include the limited public comp coverage and the absence of late-stage (Series F+) private comparables in the filtered peer set.",
