      "narrative": "Overland AI is a Series A defense and security company founded by Byron Boots, Greg Okopal, and Stephanie Bonk, having raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 11 companies in the Defense & Security sector at the same or adjacent stage, comprising 2 public comparables and 8 private peers including Singularity, NODA AI, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Castelion.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $40M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, implies an $80M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 11-company comp set yields a $1.0B implied value, with the peer universe ranging from $125M at the low end to $3.0B at the high end. Notable peers in the Series B stage include Dream Security ($3.0B), Allen Control Systems ($2.2B), Harmattan AI ($1.4B), Code Metal ($1.2B), and Twenty ($1.0B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $68M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $540M. The substantial spread reflects uncertainty around Overland AI's relative position within a heterogeneous peer set. Key sensitivities include the company's realized progress on product differentiation, customer concentration, and how tightly the peer cohort actually reflects Overland AI's growth trajectory and market opportunity.",
