      "narrative": "Theseus is a Seed-stage defense and security company that has raised $4.3M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in Defense & Security, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Castelion.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression analysis uses the $4.3M raised as a base and applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $11M. Peer-Median analysis examines three same-sector companies at Seed or Series A stages: UFORCE ($1.0B), Singularity ($400M), and NODA AI ($125M). The median valuation of this peer cohort is $400M, establishing a range from $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a range of $9M to $460M, with a median point of $205M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty inherent in early-stage defense-tech valuations, where funding velocity and strategic importance can diverge sharply from traditional metrics. Key sensitivities include: the degree to which Theseus's technical capabilities match those of Seed-stage peers like UFORCE versus earlier-stage comparables; whether subsequent funding demonstrates investor conviction at the upper end of the peer range; and whether Defense & Security valuations sustain current multiples. The Stage-Progression floor of $9M represents minimum reference value; the peer median of $205M should anchor base-case consideration.",
