      "narrative": "NuScale Power operates in the nuclear energy sector, a space populated by 11 identifiable peers\u20143 public and 8 private. The company has raised over $600M to date. The peer universe includes public comparables trading under OKLO, NNE, and SMR, alongside private competitors including Oklo, X-Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nThe peer-median method is not applicable to this valuation. The nuclear energy sector contains only six same-sector peers overall, and of these, fewer than three meet the filters required for a statistically reliable median calculation (same stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier). Relying on a broader all-sector median would introduce unacceptable distortion given the specialized nature of nuclear technology, capital intensity, and regulatory environment that differentiate this sector from other energy businesses.\n\nWithout a sufficiently dense peer cohort meeting narrow stage and tier criteria, this analysis cannot triangulate a supported valuation range via comparable company methods alone. Resolution would require either: (1) expansion of the peer set through identification of additional same-stage or adjacent-stage nuclear energy companies; (2) application of alternative methods such as precedent transaction analysis, discounted cash flow modeling, or sum-of-the-parts analysis using disclosed project pipelines and development timelines; or (3) explicit reliance on the public trading multiples of OKLO, NNE, and SMR, with documentation of stage and risk differential adjustments. The illiquidity discount and pre-revenue or early-revenue profile of most private peers remains a material valuation uncertainty.",
