      "narrative": "Type One Energy is a Series B nuclear energy company founded by David Anderson, Chris Hegna, and John Canik, having raised over $100M to date. The valuation assessment draws from a comp universe of 11 peers across nuclear energy\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private entities including Valar Atomics, Helion, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nA stage-progression methodology applies a 1.9x multiplier to the $100M total raised proxy, reflecting typical venture capital step-up economics from Series B to subsequent stages, yielding an implied valuation of $190M. A peer-median approach was not applicable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow nuclear energy set; while 6 same-sector peers exist, clustering by stage and valuation tier produced fewer than three datapoints, making sector-wide median comparison unreliable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $162M to $218M, with a median of $190M. This range reflects the constraints of a single methodological input and limited granular peer data at Type One Energy's specific stage and scale. Key uncertainties include the absence of tighter peer comparability in Series B nuclear energy financing, materiality of technology differentiation within the sector, and typical market volatility in pre-revenue frontier energy valuations. Additional financing data or revenue/milestone disclosure would strengthen conviction in this range.",
