      "narrative": "Nano Nuclear Energy, a Seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Jay Jiang Yu, is valued at $808M post-money following $600M+ in total funding. The nuclear energy sector comp universe includes 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms, including Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Fuse Energy.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the applicable triangulation method here. Using the $808M last post-money valuation as a base and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for progression from Seed to the subsequent stage yields $2.0B. Peer-median comparison was not viable; while 5 nuclear energy peers exist in the broader database, insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables with similar valuation tiers met the threshold for meaningful cross-sectional analysis.\n\nThe valuation analysis supports a range of $1.7B to $2.3B, centered on a $2.0B median. This represents modest upside from the current $808M valuation under the assumption of continued execution and market progression. Key uncertainties include the thinness of the comparable set\u2014only one applicable method could be reliably applied\u2014and the lack of historical precedent for later-stage nuclear energy financings in this cycle. Investors should view this range as contingent on the company's ability to de-risk core technical and regulatory milestones before next fundraising.",
