      "narrative": "Proteus Space is a Series A space & aerospace company founded by David Kervin and Andrew Shapiro that has raised $14.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers spanning the sector, including Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space at comparable or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $17M total-raised proxy as a baseline and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A to the next stage, implying a $34M valuation. Peer-median analysis across 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring is not applicable because target revenue is not on file, precluding application of the 24.4x sector P/S median observed across public Space & Aerospace peers.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a range of $29M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $667M. The wide dispersion reflects tension between the stage-progression floor and the peer-median anchor, which assumes rapid scaling. Key uncertainties include target revenue trajectory, differentiation relative to better-capitalized peers, and execution risk at the Series A stage. Resolution of stage-specific milestones will be critical to disambiguating the valuation range at the next financing event.",
