      "narrative": "Terran Robotics is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Zach Dwiel and Danny Weddle. The company has raised $256K to date. The relevant comp universe spans Robotics & Manufacturing, which includes one public company (277810.KQ) and eight private peers including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nValuation analysis was constrained by data availability. A peer-median method proved inapplicable: while 11 same-sector peers exist, the narrow filters for stage, adjacent stage, and valuation tier yielded insufficient datapoints (fewer than three required for statistical reliability). Stage-progression analysis was therefore the sole applicable triangulation method. Using $256K total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage progression implied a valuation of $640K.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $544K to $736K, with a median of $640K, derived from \u00b115% variance around the single method output. This range should be treated as provisional given reliance on a single valuation lever. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 2.5x multiplier to Terran's specific stage velocity and market conditions, the lack of comparable seed-stage transactions in the robotics subsector, and limited visibility into company-specific metrics (burn rate, customer traction, intellectual property). Widening the comp set or obtaining additional transaction data would materially improve confidence.",
