      "narrative": "Astera Labs is a publicly traded semiconductor company founded by Jitendra Mohan, Sanjay Gajendra, and Casey Morrison, having raised $713M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a universe of 4 same-sector, same-stage public peers in Chips & Semiconductors: Cerebras ($39.2B), Credo Semiconductor ($35.8B), Ouster ($2.3B), and Aeva Technologies ($1.1B).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach given the target's public status and available comparables. The median valuation across these 4 peers is $19.0B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $39.2B. A public-comp anchoring method using price-to-sales multiples from semiconductor sector leaders (NVDA, AMD, ALAB) could theoretically apply, with the sector median P/S at 18.9x; however, this method cannot be executed without the target's disclosed revenue figures.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $16.2B to $21.9B, centered on the peer median of $19.0B. This range reflects the dispersion observed across the peer set, where valuations vary significantly based on commercial traction and market positioning. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the peer group\u2014the wide range ($1.1B to $39.2B) suggests heterogeneity in business model and growth profile\u2014and the unavailability of revenue data to cross-check multiples-based approaches. Additional financial metrics on profitability and growth rate would sharpen the valuation estimate.",
