      "narrative": "Rocket Factory Augsburg is a Series B-stage space & aerospace company that has raised $80M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and SpaceX, with particular focus on 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $80M total raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implying $152M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector companies\u2014Sierra Space ($8.0B, Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B, Series C)\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.1B to $8.0B. Public comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not disclosed. The median of public Space & Aerospace comparables trades at 24.4x P/S, but this multiple is not actionable without revenue data.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $129M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $901M. The wide dispersion reflects uncertainty in stage-to-stage progression assumptions and peer selection heterogeneity, particularly the inclusion of significantly later-stage players. Revenue disclosure and clarity on development milestones would narrow this band materially.",
