      "narrative": "Verkor is a Series C climate and energy technology company that has raised over \u20ac3.0B to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private companies and 1 public equity (LNZA) operating in the same sector at similar stages, including peers such as KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $3.0B raised proxy, yielding $5.1B. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range from $700M (Amogy) to $3.0B (KoBold Metals). The methodological divergence\u2014$5.1B versus $1.0B\u2014reflects tension between capital-intensity benchmarking and peer trading multiples.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $850M (low) to $5.9B (high), with a median of $3.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around two drivers: (1) stage-transition probability and timing, which anchors the upside; and (2) peer comparability on unit economics and path to profitability, which anchors the downside. The peer-median sits materially below the stage-progression output, suggesting either that raised capital has not yet translated to proportional value creation, or that stage-comparable peers trade at a discount to capital intensity. Further clarity on capital deployment efficiency and revenue traction would narrow this band.",
