      "narrative": "Synhelion, a Series C climate and energy company founded by Gianluca Ambrosetti, has raised $80M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy) valued between $700M and $3.0B, plus one public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression modeling uses $80M in total capital raised as a proxy for current valuation and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $136M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the median valuation of the three-company Climate & Energy Series C cohort, which stands at $1.0B, reflecting typical market pricing for later-stage frontier-tech operators at this maturity level.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $116M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $568M. This wide spread reflects material valuation uncertainty inherent in early-stage climate tech: stage-progression conservatively assumes modest progression from capital deployed, while peer-median reflects market-clearing prices for comparable but not identical technology risk profiles. Key uncertainties include technology readiness relative to peer set, capital efficiency relative to deployment capital, and near-term funding milestones that would reset expected follow-on valuation multiples.",
