      "narrative": "Saltfoss Energy is a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Troels Schonfeldt that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers across public and private markets: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy, all operating in the nuclear energy sector at seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $40M in total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression, implies an $80M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Valar Atomics ($6.0B, Series B), Nano Nuclear Energy ($808M, Seed), and Fuse Energy ($200M, Series A)\u2014yields a median of $808M, with a range spanning $200M to $6.0B.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $68M to $929M, with a median of $444M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and maturity differences within the peer set, particularly the outsized valuation of Valar Atomics at Series B. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to peers, path to revenue, and capital requirements through commercialization. The $200M\u2013$808M band represents the most defensible range, anchored by same-stage and earlier-stage nuclear peers.",
