      "narrative": "D-Orbit is a Series C space & aerospace company founded by Luca Rossettini and Renato Panesi that has raised $166M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of seven private peers in the same sector and adjacent stages (Sierra Space, Impulse Space, Apex Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Varda Space Industries, and two others), plus five public Space & Aerospace benchmarks (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement, yielding $282M. Peer-median analysis across the seven same-sector comparables produces a $2.0B implied valuation, with the peer set ranging from $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; the sector median P/S of 24.4x across public peers is not actionable without D-Orbit's disclosed revenue. \n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $240M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.1B. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty: stage-based mechanics point toward the lower end, while peer positioning\u2014especially relative to series-equivalent and later-stage competitors\u2014supports the higher range. Capital efficiency, revenue generation, and competitive moat definition remain the key variables driving placement within this band.",
