      "narrative": "Tevel Aerobotics, a Series B-stage drone and autonomous systems company, has raised $42.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of eight private companies in the Drones & Autonomous sector, including Elroy Air, Waymo, Wayve, Zipline, and Joby Aviation. No public comparables exist in this narrow sector definition.\n\nStage-progression methodology is applicable here. Using total capital raised ($43M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage progression yields an implied valuation of $81M. This method directly reflects observed capital-deployment patterns within the sector. Peer-median analysis could not be applied: while seven same-sector peers exist, insufficient depth at the same stage, adjacent stages, or similar valuation tiers (fewer than three datapoints in any filtered subset) makes median-based triangulation unreliable and subject to undue outlier bias.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $69M to $93M, with a central estimate of $81M. This single-method result carries meaningful uncertainty. The primary gap is the absence of statistically robust peer multiples at Tevel's precise stage and scale. Confidence in the midpoint depends on the validity of the 1.9x step-up assumption for this specific subsector; frontier-stage autonomous systems may experience different progression rates than broader venture cohorts. Additional certainty would require either expansion of the peer set or observation of subsequent transaction activity within the Drones & Autonomous sector.",
