      "narrative": "Innospace, a public-stage space and aerospace company founded by Kim Soo-Jong, has raised $80M+ to date. The valuation analysis relies on a peer-median approach anchored to five same-sector, same-stage comparables: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across these five public space & aerospace companies is $7.6B, with a range spanning $840M at the low end (Astroscale) to $1.6T at the high end (SpaceX). This wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity within the sector\u2014differences in scale, capability maturity, and market position. A revenue-based P/S multiple approach cannot be applied, as Innospace's revenue is not disclosed and private companies rarely make this metric available; the public space & aerospace sector median P/S of 24.4x remains inaccessible without revenue data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6.4B to $8.7B, with a median point estimate of $7.6B. This estimate carries material uncertainty given reliance on a single method and the extreme valuational spread within the peer set. The wide gap between SpaceX and Astroscale suggests that peer-median anchoring should be treated as directional rather than precise. Additional clarity on Innospace's revenue, customer concentration, and development stage would refine this estimate materially.",
