      "narrative": "Silicon Box, a Series B-stage semiconductor company founded by Han Byung Joon, Sehat Sutardja, and Weili Dai, has raised over $200M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 3 public semiconductor names (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers in chips and semiconductors at similar or adjacent stages, including Positron AI, Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, and Etched.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method uses the $200M raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $380M. The peer-median method anchors to 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Rebellions ($2.3B, Series A), d-Matrix ($2.0B, Series A), Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), and DEEPX ($529M, Series C)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.5B. Public company anchoring via P/S multiples (median 18.9x across the three public tickers) cannot be applied due to the absence of Silicon Box's revenue disclosure, typical for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $323M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $940M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around growth trajectory and whether comparables like Rebellions and d-Matrix at higher valuations constitute true peers or represent outliers driven by investor enthusiasm for the sector.",
