      "narrative": "Satellogic is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised $262M to date. The valuation analysis benchmarks against a universe of five same-sector, same-stage public peers: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nA peer-median approach is applicable and forms the primary valuation method. The median valuation across these five comparables is $7.6B, with a range spanning $840M at the low end (Astroscale) to $1.6T at the high end (SpaceX). This wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in company scale, technology maturity, and commercial traction within the sector. A revenue-multiple approach using the Space & Aerospace public median of 24.4x P/S could not be applied, as Satellogic's revenue is not on file.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $6.4B to $8.7B, centered on the peer median of $7.6B. This single-method result carries inherent uncertainty given the small peer cohort and substantial valuation spread within it. The analysis is particularly sensitive to whether Satellogic's business profile aligns closer to higher-revenue operators like Rocket Lab or lower-capitalization peers like Astroscale. Additional clarity on revenue, customer concentration, and launch cadence would narrow the range materially.",
