      "narrative": "Dawn Aerospace, a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $25M to date, sits within a competitive frontier-tech sector anchored by five public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and eight private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and SpaceX. Two valuation methods are applicable to this analysis.\n\nStage-progression methodology, using the $25M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $48M. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables produces a $1.6B implied valuation. The peer set ranges from $1.1B (Skyryse, Series C) to $8.0B (Sierra Space, Series C), with Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B and Aalyria at $1.3B serving as closer stage comparables. Public-comp anchoring, using the sector's 24.4x P/S median across six tickers, cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue data.\n\nTriangulation across the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $40M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $849M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Dawn Aerospace's competitive positioning within the peer set and stage-appropriate risk adjustment. Key unknowns include revenue trajectory, technical execution risk, and market timing relative to the broader space-tech cycle.",
