      "narrative": "RobCo is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Roman H\u00f6lzl, Paul Maroldt, and Constantin Dresel, having raised $160M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014including adjacent-stage operators like Humanoid, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo methods triangulate RobCo's value. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $160M raised proxy, implying a $320M valuation. Peer-median methodology samples five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies with a median valuation of $1.6B and a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B, reflecting the dispersion between Seed-stage Walden Robotics ($1.1B) and Series B operators like Generalist AI ($2.0B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $272M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $985M. The wide dispersion reflects uncertainty around RobCo's stage positioning relative to peers\u2014whether it sits closer to early-stage or Series B-equivalent traction\u2014and the heterogeneity of robotics valuations at this market moment. The peer-median method suggests valuation clustering near $1.6B, while stage-progression implies a more conservative trajectory. Key uncertainties include RobCo's specific revenue and deployment metrics relative to the named peer set and the sustainability of current frontier-robotics market multiples.",
