      "narrative": "Deep Isolation, founded by Elizabeth Muller and Richard A. Muller, is a Series A nuclear energy company that has raised $26M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers across the nuclear energy sector\u20143 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Oklo\u2014spanning seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using the $26M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage step-ups, implies a $52M valuation. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Valar Atomics at $6.0B Series B, Nano Nuclear Energy at $808M Seed, and Fuse Energy at $200M Series A) yields a median of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects significant heterogeneity in the nuclear energy private market at this stage.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated range of $44M (low) to $929M (high), with a median of $430M. The substantial gap between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects uncertainty around Deep Isolation's relative competitive position within the sector. Key uncertainties include technology differentiation relative to the peer set, path to commercialization timelines, and the current trajectory of nuclear energy sector funding momentum.",
