      "narrative": "Long Wall is a late-stage Defense & Security company founded by Dan Piemont and Harry O'Hanley (both ex-SpaceX and ex-Morgan Stanley) that has raised $544M to date. The valuation universe comprises 10 private peers (including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI) and 2 public comparables (DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS), though a sufficiently narrow peer set at the same stage and valuation tier does not exist within the Defense & Security sector.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the applicable triangulation approach. Using $544M in total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical for late-stage advancement yields an implied value of $653M. A sensitivity band around this central estimate\u2014reflecting execution risk and the thin peer comparability\u2014ranges from $555M (conservative, 1.02x raised) to $751M (optimistic, 1.38x raised).\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $555M to $751M, with a median point of $653M. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct late-stage Defense & Security comparables with disclosed metrics, reliance on stage-progression heuristics rather than revenue or margin multiples, and limited visibility into Long Wall's revenue scale relative to the peer universe. Additional revenue and growth trajectory data would substantially narrow this range.",
