      "narrative": "GrayMatter Robotics is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $70M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private peers and 1 public company in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods apply. Stage-progression analysis anchors to the last known post-money valuation of $300M and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding $570M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B)\u2014producing a median of $1.8B with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $484M to $2.0B, with a median of $1.2B. The wide spread reflects material tension between the stage-progression method, which conservatively extrapolates from the last funding round, and peer multiples, which suggest substantially higher valuations in the current market. Key uncertainties include (1) whether peer comparables appropriately control for GrayMatter's revenue traction and product maturity relative to the sample, (2) the timing and market conditions of the target's last financing, and (3) burn rate and path to profitability relative to peers.",
