      "narrative": "Pano AI is a Series B climate and energy technology company seeking valuation in a sector containing one public comparable (LNZA) and eight material private peers. The private peer set includes advanced materials and alternative energy developers at Series C stage, among them KoBold Metals ($3.0B), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B), and Amogy ($700M).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis using the company's last post-money valuation of $500M and a typical Series B-to-next-stage multiplier of 1.9x yields $950M. Peer-median analysis across the three most direct Climate & Energy comparables in the same or adjacent stage produces a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. These approaches triangulate to a low estimate of $808M, a median of $975M, and a high of $1.1B.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $800M to $1.1B, centered near $975M. Key uncertainties include the wide dispersion in peer valuations\u2014a three-fold range suggests material differentiation by technology maturity, capital intensity, or commercial traction\u2014and the limited applicability of public comparables in this nascent sector. Relative to the $89M raised to date, this implies a post-money valuation roughly 10\u201312x cumulative investment.",
