      "narrative": "Collaborative Robotics, founded by Brad Porter, is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $150M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (277810.KQ), with primary reliance on three same-stage, same-sector peers: Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B).\n\nTwo methods triangulate the valuation. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier to the last known post-money valuation of $500M, yielding $950M. Peer-median analysis across the three robotics comparables produces a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.6B to $2.0B. The peer-median approach carries greater weight given the direct comparability of stage and sector.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $808M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $1.4B. The width of this range reflects meaningful uncertainty around capital deployment pace, technical risk, and market adoption rates specific to autonomous systems in manufacturing. The gap between stage-progression ($950M) and peer-median ($1.8B) suggests either that Collaborative Robotics operates at a discount to peer valuations or that the peer set may reflect above-median execution. Further diligence on ARR growth, customer concentration, and hardware margins would narrow this band.",
