      "narrative": "Chef Robotics is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Rajat Bhageria that has raised $65.6M to date. The valuation analysis relies on a peer set of 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables spanning Series A through Series B, including Humanoid ($1.4B), Dexterity ($1.6B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Generalist AI ($2.0B), alongside 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline of $15M and applying a 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, yields $30M. Peer-median valuation across the five robotics comparables produces $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $2.0B. This wide range reflects stage heterogeneity within the peer set, with Series B companies commanding significantly higher valuations than Series A peers.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $26M (low), $840M (median), and $1.9B (high). The 70x spread between stage-progression and peer-median methods reflects fundamental tension between two signals: the company's actual capital deployed and the market's current pricing of advanced robotics companies at later stages. Key uncertainties include whether Chef Robotics' operational progress and addressable market justify peer valuations skewed toward Series B, and whether the peer set adequately reflects sector-specific risk factors or unit economics. Resolution requires visibility into revenue traction, customer concentration, and capital efficiency relative to comparables.",
