      "narrative": "LeoLabs is a Series B space and aerospace company that has raised $94M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and SpaceX, though public multiples cannot be applied without disclosed revenue.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $94M total raised proxy, implying a $179M valuation. Peer-median analysis across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies yields a $1.6B implied valuation. The peer set spans $1.1B (Skyryse, Series C) to $8.0B (Sierra Space, Series C), with adjacent-stage Series B comparables at $2.0B (Cowboy Space) and $1.3B (Aalyria). Public Space & Aerospace comps show a 24.4x median P/S multiple but cannot be applied given LeoLabs' undisclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $152M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $914M across the two applicable methods. Material uncertainty stems from the wide spread between stage-progression and peer-median approaches\u2014reflecting both LeoLabs' early funding relative to later-stage comparables and inherent dispersion in space-sector valuations. Revenue visibility and the company's specific position within orbital debris/space situational awareness would sharpen this estimate materially.",
