      "narrative": "Locus Robotics, a Series F robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $480M+, is currently valued at $2.0B post-money. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable set of 10 same-sector peers at similar valuation tiers, comprising 1 public company and 9 private firms including Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), and Dexterity ($1.6B, Series B). The peer set ranges from $1.0B to $2.3B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a typical 1.3x step-up multiplier from Series F to the next funding stage, yielding $2.6B. Peer-median analysis across the 10-company set produces $1.6B, reflecting the distribution of valuations across varying development stages within the robotics sector. The geometric mean of these two results anchors the analysis.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $1.4B to $3.0B, with a median of $2.1B. This range reflects material variance between forward-looking step-up assumptions and current-stage peer comparables. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate and profitability trajectory relative to peers, customer concentration, and market timing in robotics deployment cycles. The current $2.0B valuation sits near the lower bound of the implied range, suggesting modest upside under stage-typical assumptions, though peer-relative valuation presents downside risk.",
