      "narrative": "Outrider is a Series D robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $262M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014one public entity and eight private firms\u2014spanning similar stages and sector focus. Key private peers include Exotec ($2.0B, Series D), Hadrian ($1.6B, Series D), Divergent ($2.3B, Series E), Agile Robots ($1.0B, Series C), and Nimble Robotics ($1.0B, Series C).\n\nTwo primary methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $262M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.5x multiplier typical for Series D progression, yielding $393M. Peer-median analysis draws from the five-company comparable set in robotics and manufacturing at same or adjacent stages, with a median valuation of $1.6B and a range of $1.0B to $2.3B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a valuation range of $334M (low) to $1.8B (high), with a median of $996M. The wide spread reflects meaningful stage and maturity variation within the peer cohort\u2014particularly the gap between Series C peers at $1.0B and Series E Divergent at $2.3B. Key uncertainties center on Outrider's relative unit economics, capital efficiency, and customer concentration relative to named peers. The peer-median method carries greater weight given direct sector and stage alignment, anchoring the analysis toward the $1.0B\u2013$1.6B range.",
