      "narrative": "Swarm Aero is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company that has raised $8M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 companies across Defense & Security\u20142 public (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $8M total raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for progression from Seed to the next stage, implying a $20M valuation. The peer-median method references 3 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: UFORCE (Seed, $1.0B), Singularity (Series A, $400M), and NODA AI (Series A, $125M). The median across these three is $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B. This method implies $400M.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $17M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $210M. The wide spread reflects substantial uncertainty inherent in valuing early-stage frontier-tech companies where comparable multiples vary significantly by funding stage and market positioning. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor; peer medians suggest material upside but depend critically on whether Swarm Aero's technology trajectory and market opportunity align with higher-valued peers versus lower-valued comparables.",
