      "narrative": "Zanskar, a Series C-stage climate and energy company founded by Carl Hoiland and Joel Edwards, has raised $180M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), alongside a broader landscape including one public comparable and eight private peers in the climate tech space.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $180M in total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, yields $306M. Peer-median analysis across the three direct comparables produces $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B reflecting meaningful dispersion in recent Climate & Energy Series C valuations. \n\nThe two methods produce a triangulated range of $260M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $653M. This wide spread\u2014spanning $840M\u2014reflects heterogeneity in the peer set and the binary tension between fundamentals-based progression and recent market comps. Key uncertainties include stage-specific capital efficiency relative to peers, technology differentiation within the Climate & Energy sector, and the sustainability of peer valuations in a fluctuating venture market. A valuation toward the median ($650M\u2013$700M) appears defensible absent material new information on Zanskar's technical or commercial position relative to named comparables.",
