      "narrative": "Kepler Communications is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $200M+ to date. Valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 13 comparable companies\u20145 public equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms at Series B through Series D stages, including Sierra Space, Impulse Space, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression modeling applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $200M total-raised proxy, yielding $340M. Peer-median anchoring across 7 same-sector comparables at matching or adjacent stages produces a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $1.15B (floor) to $8.0B (Sierra Space ceiling). The public-comp method using a 24.4x price-to-sales median across the five listed peers cannot be applied in the absence of Kepler's disclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $289M to $2.3B, with a median of $1.2B. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty around stage-appropriate multiples in this sector\u2014stage-progression implies a more conservative floor, while peer-median gravitates toward upper-quartile comparable valuations. Key uncertainties include Kepler's revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and technology differentiation relative to the peer set, particularly high-valuation outliers like Sierra Space at $8.0B.",
