      "narrative": "Reaction Dynamics is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised C$38M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 8 private and 5 public peers in the Space & Aerospace sector, including private companies such as SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and ICEYE, and public comparables including RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, and SATL (median P/S: 24.4x).\n\nTwo quantitative methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding an implied valuation of $76M based on the $38M total raised as a proxy for current value. Peer-median triangulation across three same-sector companies at comparable or adjacent stages\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B, Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B, Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B, Seed)\u2014produces a median of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public comp anchoring cannot be applied because Reaction Dynamics' revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $65M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $688M. This wide spread reflects stage and maturity variance in the comp set; the stage-progression method anchors conservatively to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects valuations of more mature Series B entrants. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate, technology differentiation relative to peers, and whether Reaction Dynamics has achieved material technical or commercial milestones post-Series A.",
