      "narrative": "Fortera, a Series C-stage climate and energy technology company that has raised $200M+, is valued against a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA). The three primary private peers\u2014KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy\u2014all operate at the Series C stage within the climate and energy sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $200M total raised as a proxy base and applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, yielding $340M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-stage, same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $1.0B, with a range from $700M (Amogy) to $3.0B (KoBold Metals). This wide spread reflects material variance in investor conviction and technology maturity within the cohort.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $289M to $1.1B, with a median of $670M. The $670M midpoint reflects tension between the conservative stage-progression approach and the elevated peer medians. Key uncertainties include whether Fortera's technology risk profile and capital efficiency align with the lower-valued peers (Amogy, Electric Hydrogen) or commands KoBold's premium. The wide peer range ($700M\u2013$3.0B) itself signals meaningful unresolved questions about differentiation and market timing in this sector.",
