      "narrative": "LanzaTech is a public-stage climate and energy company founded by Sean Simpson and Richard Forster, having raised over $500M to date. The peer universe consists of 1 public comparable and 8 private frontier-tech companies in the Climate & Energy sector, with QuantumScape, Enovix, and Solid Power serving as the primary public references.\n\nOur valuation analysis applies a peer-median approach across three same-sector, same-stage comparables. QuantumScape trades at $3.6B, Enovix at $1.0B, and Solid Power at $504M, establishing a peer range of $504M to $3.6B with a median valuation of $1.0B. This method yields an implied valuation of $1.0B for LanzaTech, the sole applicable triangulation method given available data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $850M to $1.1B, centered on $1.0B. This represents a substantial step-up from LanzaTech's current market capitalization of $72.51M. Key uncertainties include the limited depth of the comparable set and the wide dispersion within the peer cohort\u2014a 7.2x spread from floor to ceiling\u2014reflecting the nascent, high-variance nature of frontier energy technology valuations. Execution risk, commercialization timelines, and capital efficiency relative to peers remain critical variables not fully captured by this peer analysis alone.",
