      "narrative": "eGenesis is a Series C-stage biotech company founded by Luhan Yang and George Church, having raised $250M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of 3 same-stage private companies in Biotech & Health (Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, New Limit) and 3 public biotech comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $250M total raised proxy, implying a valuation of $425M. Peer-median analysis references 3 same-sector, same-stage private companies with a median valuation of $3.8B, though the range is wide ($3.1B to $10.3B). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied given the absence of revenue data for the target. The triangulation of these two methods yields a low estimate of $361M, a median of $2.1B, and a high estimate of $4.4B.\n\nThe median valuation of $2.1B reflects meaningful dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results. Stage-progression yields a more conservative estimate tied to capital deployed, while peer-median reflects market multiples paid for similar-stage biotech assets. Key uncertainties include the wide peer range ($3.1B\u2013$10.3B), driven primarily by Colossal's $10.3B valuation, and the absence of revenue or near-term commercial milestones for anchoring. The analysis supports a range of $361M to $4.4B, with $2.1B as the central estimate.",
