      "narrative": "Hexium is a seed-stage nuclear energy company founded by Charlie Jarrott and Jacob Peterson that has raised $10M+. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 11 nuclear energy peers: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private entities including Nano Nuclear Energy, Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, and X-Energy.\n\nStage-progression valuation is the primary applicable method, using the $10M total raised as a proxy base and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement. This yields an implied valuation of $25M. Peer-median analysis was not applicable due to insufficient narrow-set comparables; while six same-sector peers exist in nuclear energy, none of the filtered subsets (same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar valuation tier) contained the minimum three datapoints required for meaningful triangulation. Applying an all-sector median would introduce unacceptable noise given the specialized nature of frontier nuclear technology.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $21M (low), $25M (median), to $29M (high), anchored entirely on the stage-progression method. The primary uncertainty stems from the scarcity of precisely comparable seed-stage nuclear companies, making the 2.5x multiplier assumption the key driver of the range. Investors should weight this analysis as preliminary pending access to tighter peer financials or additional data on Hexium's technical and commercial progress relative to the comp set.",
