      "narrative": "Starcloud, a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Philip Johnston, Ezra Feilden, and Adi Oltean, carries a current post-money valuation of $1.1B on $170M raised. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 8 private companies in the same sector and valuation tier, alongside 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) for sectoral context.\n\nTwo quantitative methods triangulate Starcloud's fair value. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implying $2.8B. Peer-median analysis across 8 same-sector private peers yields $1.8B, with the peer set ranging from $840M to $4.3B. Public-comp anchoring, while applicable to the sector (median P/S of 24.4x across 6 tickers), cannot be deployed for Starcloud absent revenue disclosure. The two applicable methods produce a triangulated range of $1.5B to $3.2B, with a median of $2.3B.\n\nThe current $1.1B valuation sits below both method results, suggesting either a discount to stage-appropriate pricing or an opportunity cost relative to peer medians. Key uncertainties include Starcloud's revenue trajectory relative to profitability comparables, and whether the peer set adequately reflects the company's specific technology and execution risk. The $1.5B\u2013$3.2B range brackets reasonable fair-value estimates pending deeper operational diligence.",
