      "narrative": "Cemvita is a Series B climate and energy company founded by Moji and Tara Karimi that has raised $30M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 private companies and 1 public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA) operating in the climate and energy sector, including stage-adjacent players like KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Amogy.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $30M total raised as a proxy base value and applying a typical 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $57M. The peer-median approach examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: KoBold Metals at $3.0B (Series C), Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B (Series C), and Amogy at $700M (Series C). The median of this cohort is $1.0B, with a stated range of $700M to $3.0B, implying $1.0B.\n\nTriangulating these two methods produces a valuation range of $48M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median of $528M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty in stage-appropriate peer selection and the applicability of later-stage comparables to a Series B asset. The peer-median method, while grounded in observable transactions, relies on only three data points in a volatile sector. Key uncertainties include technology maturity, path to unit economics, and sector-specific capital intensity relative to peers.",
