      "narrative": "Forge Nano is a Series C-stage climate and energy company that has raised $40M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of three same-sector, same-stage private companies (KoBold Metals at $3.0B, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B, and Amogy at $700M), alongside one public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA) and a broader universe of eight private frontier-tech peers.\n\nTwo methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the $40M raised as a proxy for pre-money valuation, applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C progression, yielding $68M. Peer-median analysis across the three same-stage, same-sector comparables produces a $1.0B implied valuation, with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. The median valuation across both methods is $534M.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $58M (floor, representing a modest premium to raised capital) to $1.1B (ceiling, anchored to the upper quartile of peer valuations). The median estimate of $534M sits materially above stage-progression but reflects the wide dispersion within the peer cohort. Key uncertainty stems from the heterogeneity of comparable companies and absence of recent transaction multiples specific to frontier-energy hardware. Capital efficiency and technology de-risking relative to peers remain primary value drivers.",
