      "narrative": "VulcanForms is a late-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by John Hart and Martin Feldmann that has raised $575M+ to date. The comparable universe consists of 9 peers across robotics and manufacturing\u20141 public and 8 private firms including Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, Generalist AI, and Bedrock Robotics\u2014though a sufficiently narrow peer set at identical stage and valuation tier does not exist for direct median benchmarking.\n\nGiven data constraints, stage-progression methodology is the primary applicable approach. Using total capital raised ($575M) as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.2x step-up multiplier typical for late-stage advancement yields an implied value of $690M. This method reflects the company's progression within its funding lifecycle but carries inherent limitations absent direct comparable transaction or earnings multiples.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $586M to $793M, with $690M as the median point. Key uncertainties include the absence of sufficient narrow-stage comparable transactions, reliance on a single triangulation method, and lack of disclosed financial metrics (revenue, EBITDA, unit economics) that would enable revenue or profitability multiple analysis. Any refinement of this range would require either additional same-stage private peer data or disclosure of financial performance metrics suitable for multiple-based approaches.",
