      "narrative": "Lumotive is a Series B semiconductor company that has raised $72M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 8 private and 3 public firms operating in Chips & Semiconductors, including peers such as Positron AI ($1.0B, Series B), Rebellions ($2.3B, Series A), and public anchors NVDA, AMD, and ALAB.\n\nTwo triangulation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement to the $72M total raised proxy, implying $137M. Peer-median anchoring across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Rebellions, d-Matrix, Positron AI, and DEEPX\u2014yields a median valuation of $1.5B, with a range spanning $529M to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 18.9x across ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied without disclosed revenue figures, a typical constraint for private companies.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $116M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $818M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around stage timing, revenue trajectory, and competitive positioning relative to the peer set. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor, while peer medians anchor toward the upper range. Key sensitivities include revenue run-rate assumptions needed to calibrate public multiples and relative product-market traction versus the Positron AI and Cerebras cohort.",
