      "narrative": "Standard Bots, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Evan Beard and David Golden, has raised $200M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison set of 3 private peers at the same stage and sector\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B)\u2014supplemented by a broader universe of 8 private robotics firms and 1 public comparable.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression, using total raised ($200M) as a value proxy and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yields $380M. Peer-median triangulation across the three same-stage, same-sector comparables produces $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.6B to $2.0B. The peer-median approach is more granular but reflects the sector's higher growth multiples at this stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $323M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median estimate of $1.1B. This wide spread reflects tension between the stage-progression method, anchored conservatively to capital deployed, and peer comparables, which price at material premiums reflecting sector momentum and the capital intensity of frontier robotics. Key uncertainties include differentiation within the peer set\u2014particularly whether Standard Bots' technology or market position warrants positioning toward the upper or lower quartile of comparables\u2014and the sustainability of current robotics sector valuations.",
