      "narrative": "Path Robotics is a Series D robotics and manufacturing automation company that has raised $271M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Divergent, Exotec, Hadrian, Agile Robots, and Nimble Robotics), alongside one public comparator, spanning valuations from $1.0B to $2.3B.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression approach, using total capital raised as a proxy base and applying a typical 1.5x Series D step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $406M. The peer-median method, anchored to the median valuation of $1.6B across the five comparable companies (range: $1.0B\u2013$2.3B), reflects market pricing for similar-stage automation and robotics businesses. This peer set includes Series D companies valued at $1.6B\u2013$2.0B (Hadrian, Exotec) and Series C unicorns at $1.0B (Agile Robots, Nimble Robotics), with one Series E reference point at $2.3B (Divergent).\n\nThe two methods produce a wide analytical range: the stage-progression method yields $406M, while peer-median supports $1.6B. A conservative triangulation across both approaches suggests a valuation corridor of $346M\u2013$1.8B, with a median point around $1.0B. Key uncertainties include Path Robotics' revenue scale and growth rate relative to peer cohort, profitability trajectory, and whether recent fundraising dynamics have shifted peer valuations materially from observable comps.",
