      "narrative": "Photonium is a Pre-Seed stage semiconductor company founded by Jennifer Song and Adam Mhatre. The company has raised $500K to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector comprises 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, SambaNova Systems, and Etched, though no peers matched narrow stage and valuation filters for direct median comparison.\n\nOf the three valuation methods tested, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($500K) as a proxy for current value and applying a standard Pre-Seed to next-stage step-up multiplier of 2.5x yields an implied valuation of $1.25M. Public Semiconductors command a median price-to-sales multiple of 18.9x (across ALAB, NVDA, AMD), but Photonium's revenue remains undisclosed, precluding public-comp anchoring. Peer-median analysis failed due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage private comparables in the Chips & Semiconductors universe.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $1.06M to $1.44M, with a median of $1.25M. This range reflects methodological constraint rather than convergence: only one method yielded usable output. Key uncertainties include actual revenue run-rate, technical differentiation relative to the identified peer set, and capital efficiency relative to stage norms. A meaningful triangulation would require either disclosed revenue data or expansion of the applicable peer cohort at this stage.",
