      "narrative": "OBSIDIA Semiconductor is a seed-stage chip design company founded by Erik Hosler and Adam Wilson, operating within a competitive landscape of 13 same-sector peers. The comparable universe includes 3 public companies (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private competitors, among them Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, SambaNova Systems, Etched, and Ayar Labs.\n\nStandard valuation triangulation proves constrained at this stage. The peer-median method is inapplicable: while 13 same-sector peers exist, filtering for stage, adjacency, and valuation tier yields insufficient datapoints (fewer than 3 required for statistical validity). Public-comp anchoring similarly cannot proceed\u2014the public semiconductor sector trades at a median 18.9x price-to-sales across the three comparable tickers, but OBSIDIA's revenue remains undisclosed, which is typical for private companies at seed stage and precludes revenue multiples analysis.\n\nThis analysis therefore cannot triangulate to a specific valuation range given available data. Any credible estimate would require either: (1) revenue guidance from OBSIDIA; (2) funding round pricing from comparable seed-stage semiconductor companies; or (3) disclosure of the company's current capitalization table. The key uncertainty is disclosure\u2014OBSIDIA has not publicly reported its most recent raise amount or pre-money valuation. Analysts should prioritize obtaining recent term sheets or investor presentations before proceeding to valuation.",
