      "narrative": "Remedy Robotics, a Series A robotics and manufacturing company, has raised $35M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of nine private firms and one public entity (ticker 277810.KQ) in the robotics sector, including peers such as Humanoid, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics across seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $35M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical for Series A progression, yielding $70M. Peer-median analysis across five same-sector comparables\u2014ranging from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B)\u2014produces a $1.6B median valuation. The disparity reflects the wide spread of development stage and maturity across the peer set, with most comparables at Series B or later.\n\nTriangulated analysis supports a range of $60M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $860M. The 31x spread between methods indicates material uncertainty. Stage-progression yields a conservative floor based on capital deployed; peer-median anchors to observed market pricing but includes later-stage firms commanding premium multiples. Key uncertainties include Remedy's product maturity relative to Series B comparables, revenue traction, and addressable market definition. A mid-range valuation of $200M\u2013$400M may better reflect Series A positioning unless the company demonstrates differentiated technical capability or revenue acceleration approaching peer benchmarks.",
