      "narrative": "Aeon Industrial is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Naweed Tahmas and Joe Cieslik that has raised $18.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector at similar or adjacent stages, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The Stage-Progression method uses the $18.6M raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical for Seed-to-next-stage advancement, yielding $46.5M. The Peer-Median method references three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, and NODA AI at $125M), producing a median valuation of $400M and a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThese methods generate a triangulated range of $40M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $223M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around market positioning and progress relative to the peer cohort. The Stage-Progression method anchors the lower bound, while the Peer-Median approach\u2014particularly the presence of UFORCE at $1.0B\u2014sets the upper bound. Key uncertainties include Aeon's technical differentiation versus established defense incumbents and the stage-appropriate revenue or funding velocity metrics that would justify placement within the peer range.",
