      "narrative": "Living Carbon is a Series A biotech company founded by Maddie Hall and Patrick Mellor, with $36M raised to date. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and Recursion Pharmaceuticals, though narrow-stage peer data proved limited.\n\nThe Stage-Progression method was the applicable triangulation approach. Using total raised ($36M) as a baseline proxy and applying a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage progression, this method implies a $72M valuation. Public-Comp Anchoring could not be applied because the target's revenue is not on file\u2014a common constraint with private companies. Peer-Median analysis was similarly inapplicable; while 7 same-sector peers exist, fewer than 3 met strict same-stage or adjacent-stage filters with comparable valuation tiers, making a narrow peer median unreliable.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $61M (low) to $83M (high), with a median of $72M. This range reflects +70% to +130% appreciation from deployed capital, consistent with early-stage risk. The primary uncertainty is the absence of revenue data and limited comparability among private peers at identical stage and scale. A subsequent valuation would benefit from revenue disclosure or additional same-stage fundraising events in the sector.",
