      "narrative": "Akash Systems is a Series B-stage aerospace company that has raised $40M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a universe of 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse) valued between $1.1B and $8.0B, as well as 5 public Space & Aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) trading at a median 24.4x price-to-sales.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the company's $40M total raised as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x Series B step-up multiplier, implies a valuation of $76M. Peer-median analysis anchors to the $1.6B median valuation across the 4 private comps in the same sector and stage, reflecting the wide dispersion from $1.1B (Skyryse) to $8.0B (Sierra Space). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied given the absence of disclosed revenue figures for this private company.\n\nThe triangulation of these two methods yields a range of $65M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $863M. The substantial gap between the stage-progression and peer-median approaches reflects the heterogeneity of Space & Aerospace valuations at Series B/C. Key uncertainties include Akash's revenue trajectory relative to peers, product differentiation within a capital-intensive sector, and the valuation volatility evident in the peer set.",
