      "narrative": "Xage Security is a Series B-stage defense and security company founded by Kamesh Raghavendra, Susanto Irwan, and Roman Arutyunov that has raised $80M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 8 private peers and 2 public companies operating in the Defense & Security sector.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, which uses the $80M total raised as a proxy and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B to subsequent-stage progression, yields $152M. Peer-median analysis across 8 same-sector, same-stage private companies produces $1.1B, with a distribution ranging from $300M (low) to $3.0B (high). Notable peers include Dream Security at $3.0B, Allen Control Systems at $2.2B, Harmattan AI at $1.4B, Code Metal at $1.2B, and Twenty at $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $129M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median of $638M. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty regarding Xage's revenue scale, market traction, and defensibility relative to the peer set. Stage-progression implies substantially lower valuation than peer median, suggesting either that Xage commands a discount to sector peers or that the peer sample skews toward later-stage or higher-revenue companies. Resolution of this gap would require assessment of revenue multiples, customer concentration, and growth trajectory relative to specific named comparables.",
