      "narrative": "Mythic is a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $125M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 8 private and 3 public semiconductor firms, anchored by same-stage peers including Tenstorrent ($2.7B, Series D) and Nearfield Instruments ($1.6B, Series D), as well as later-stage benchmarks Etched ($5.0B, Series E) and Ayar Labs ($3.8B, Series E).\n\nTwo methods apply to this valuation. Stage-progression anchors on total capital raised ($125M) and applies a typical Series D step-up multiplier of 1.5x, implying $188M. Peer-median triangulation across the 5 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median of $2.7B, with a range spanning $529M (DEEPX, Series C) to $5.0B (Etched, Series E). Public comp anchoring via price-to-sales (median 18.9x across ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue. The stage-progression and peer-median methods produce a triangulated valuation range of $159M (low) to $3.1B (high), with a median of $1.4B. Key uncertainties center on where within the peer band Mythic's traction, IP strength, and go-to-market readiness position it relative to Tenstorrent and Nearfield Instruments.",
