      "narrative": "Xsight Labs is a Series D semiconductor company that has raised $281M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 8 private frontier-chip firms at Series C through Series E stages\u2014including Tenstorrent, Nearfield Instruments, Ayar Labs, and Etched\u2014plus 3 public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement to the $281M raised proxy, implying $422M. Peer-median analysis across the 5 most relevant private comparables (Series C\u2013E, same sector) yields a median valuation of $2.7B, with a range spanning $529M to $5.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not available. Public semiconductor multiples (18.9x EV/Sales across the three tickers) lack a revenue anchor to deploy.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is $358M (low) to $3.1B (high), with a median of $1.6B. The wide dispersion reflects genuine uncertainty inherent to early-stage frontier semiconductors, where revenue traction and technical differentiation remain unproven at scale. The peer-median approach is most defensible given stage alignment with Tenstorrent ($2.7B) and Nearfield ($1.6B). Key sensitivities include revenue realization timelines and the ultimate viability of the technical approach relative to better-capitalized competitors.",
