      "narrative": "Orbit Fab is a Series A space technology company that has raised $28.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public equities (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers operating in Space & Aerospace, including Rocket Lab and Planet Labs. The peer set spans seed through Series B stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $28.5M raised proxy, yielding $57M. Peer-median methodology examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B (Series B), Aalyria at $1.3B (Series B), and Starcloud at $1.1B (Seed). The median across these three peers is $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B\u2013$2.0B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiple (sector median 24.4x across 6 tickers) was not applicable due to absence of disclosed revenue for the target. \n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $48M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $678M. The wide dispersion reflects the tension between capital-raised-based methods and peer multiples in an early-stage, pre-revenue context. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, capital efficiency relative to comparables, and whether Orbit Fab's specific subsector focus commands a premium or discount within the broader aerospace ecosystem.",
