      "narrative": "Starfish Space is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company founded by Austin Link and Trevor Bennett with $100M+ in total raised. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public and 8 private frontier-tech peers in the same sector, including adjacent-stage companies like Sierra Space ($8.0B Series C), Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Skyryse ($1.1B Series C).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $100M raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B step-ups, implies a valuation of $190M. Peer-median analysis across the four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comps yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied; while the Space & Aerospace sector trades at a 24.4x median price-to-sales multiple across 6 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), the target's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated range is $162M to $1.9B, with a median of $920M. This wide spread reflects the significant variance in comparable valuations and stage-dependent uncertainty. The stage-progression method suggests a floor; the peer-median suggests the center. Key uncertainties include whether Starfish Space's operational traction and unit economics align more closely with early-stage or growth-stage comparables, and whether the outlier valuations (particularly Sierra Space at $8B) reflect sector-specific tailwinds applicable here.",
