      "narrative": "Koloma is a Series B-stage climate and energy company founded by Tom Darrah, Pete Johnson, and Paul Harraka that has raised $245M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private peers (KoBold Metals at $3.0B Series C, Electric Hydrogen at $1.0B Series C, and Amogy at $700M Series C), supplemented by a broader set of nine private and one public comparable in the climate and energy technology space.\n\nTwo primary valuation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses the $245M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $466M. The peer-median approach benchmarks Koloma against the three most comparable financings, which show a median valuation of $1.0B with a range spanning $700M to $3.0B. This reflects the wide dispersion typical of early-stage climate tech, where technology differentiation and market timing drive significant valuation variance.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods supports a valuation range of $396M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median point of $733M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around Koloma's specific technology, capital efficiency relative to peers, and market timing for its particular climate solution. Stage progression and peer multiples diverge meaningfully, suggesting that endpoint scenarios depend heavily on near-term technical validation and capital deployment efficiency.",
