      "narrative": "Synchron is a Series D-stage biotech and health company that has raised $200M+ to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private peers in the Biotech & Health sector, with particular focus on 3 same-stage companies: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo applicable methods were deployed. Stage-progression analysis, anchored to the $200M total raised as a proxy for post-Series C value, applies a 1.5x step-up multiplier typical of Series D advancement, yielding $300M. Peer-median valuation across the three same-sector comparables produces a $3.8B midpoint, with a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring was not applicable due to absence of disclosed revenue data for the target. The three public biotech tickers show a median P/S multiple of 8.1x, but cannot be applied without the target's revenue.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods supports a valuation range of $255M (conservative floor using stage-progression adjusted downward) to $4.4B (upside case), with a median of $2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty around Synchron's progress relative to peer cohorts\u2014particularly the wide spread among the three direct comparables ($3.1B to $10.3B)\u2014and the absence of revenue visibility. Key sensitivities include clinical advancement stage and capital efficiency relative to peers.",
