      "narrative": "Freenome, a public-stage biotech and health company founded by Gabriel Otte, has raised $1.3B+ and carries a current valuation of $1.1B. The valuation assessment draws from a comparable universe of 3 same-sector, same-stage public peers: Recursion Pharmaceuticals ($1.6B), Alto Neuroscience ($1.0B), and Eikon Therapeutics ($539M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach, given the availability of stage-matched comparables within Biotech & Health. The median valuation across these three peers is $1.0B, with a range spanning $539M to $1.6B. A public-comp anchoring method using sector price-to-sales multiples (8.1x median across 3 public tickers: RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) cannot be applied, as Freenome's revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe single-method triangulation supports a valuation range of $884M to $1.2B, centered on a median of $1.0B. The current $1.1B valuation sits modestly above the peer median, within the upper quartile of the range. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue data (precluding multiple-based methods), limited public-comp depth in the subsector, and the company's stage dynamics post-public listing. The valuation appears defensible relative to near-peer cohort, though range width reflects material estimation risk inherent in biotech early-stage comparables.",
