      "narrative": "Precision Neuroscience is a Series C-stage biotech company that has raised $180M to date. Valuation assessment relies on a peer universe of 3 public comparables (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage peers in Biotech & Health, with particular reference to same-stage private companies including Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier to the $180M total raised proxy, implying a $306M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector, same-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range spanning $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring using the Biotech & Health sector P/S median of 8.1x cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures.\n\nTriangulation across these two methods supports a valuation range of $260M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.1B. The wide dispersion reflects material variance in peer outcomes at Series C stage within the sector. Stage-progression provides a conservative floor; peer median valuations evidence substantial valuation expansion potential. Key uncertainties include the target's clinical progress, competitive positioning within the peer set, and the timing and structure of the next financing event.",
