      "narrative": "HyImpulse is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac74 million to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 4 private companies at Series B and Series C stages (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, and Skyryse), as well as 5 public comparables in the Space & Aerospace sector (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage step-ups, yielding $141 million. Peer-median valuation across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies produces $1.6 billion, with a range of $1.1 billion to $8.0 billion. Public-comp anchoring using a 24.4x price-to-sales median across the 6 public tickers cannot be applied without disclosure of HyImpulse's revenue.\n\nThese two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $120 million (low) to $1.9 billion (high), with a median of $895 million. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression suggests a modest step-up from capital deployed, while peer multiples are heavily influenced by Sierra Space's $8.0 billion valuation, which pulls the dataset ceiling substantially higher. Resolution of this gap depends on visibility into HyImpulse's revenue trajectory, customer commitments, and technology maturity relative to the peer set.",
