      "narrative": "Isomorphic Labs, a Series B biotech and health company founded by Demis Hassabis, is evaluated against a comp universe of 3 public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and 8 private-stage companies in the same sector, including Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x multiplier to the company's $2.7B total capital raised, implying a valuation of $5.1B. Peer-median anchoring uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $3.1B to $10.3B; the median across this set is $3.8B. Public-comp P/S anchoring cannot be applied due to the absence of disclosed revenue for the private target. Public peers trade at a median 8.1x P/S, but this method yields no actionable result without revenue data.\n\nThe triangulation of these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $3.2B to $5.9B, with a median implied value of $4.5B. The spread reflects material dispersion in peer valuations\u2014particularly the $10.3B outlier in Colossal Biosciences\u2014and inherent uncertainty in stage-progression multipliers for early-stage biotech. Key sensitivities include the relevance of Series C comparables to a Series B company and the stability of capital-raise proxies as valuation anchors in pre-revenue or early-revenue contexts.",
