      "narrative": "Basecamp Research is a Series B biotech company founded by Oliver Vince and Glen Gowers that has raised $85M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 8 private and 3 public companies in Biotech & Health, including Series C-stage comparables Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier to the $85M raised proxy, implying a $162M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the three same-sector comparable companies yields a median valuation of $3.8B, with a range of $3.1B to $10.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because Basecamp's revenue is not on file. The peer-median result reflects later-stage (Series C) comparables and likely introduces upward bias relative to Basecamp's current stage.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across two methods supports a valuation range of $137M (low) to $4.4B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The wide spread reflects material tension between stage-based and peer-median approaches. Key uncertainties include Basecamp's revenue trajectory, clinical progress, and whether peer valuations from Series C rounds remain comparable to a Series B raise. Stage-progression alone suggests $162M; peer-adjusted discount to reflect stage gap would narrow the range materially.",
