      "narrative": "Candela is a Series C\u2013stage transportation company that has raised \u20ac129M+ to date. The transportation technology sector includes eight private comparable companies (Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Slate Auto, ZeroAvia, and others) and no public peers suitable for direct valuation benchmarking. The narrow peer set at Candela's specific stage and valuation tier precludes a statistically reliable peer-median approach.\n\nValuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement. Using the \u20ac129M raised as a value proxy, this method implies a valuation of $219M. A sensitivity analysis around this multiplier\u2014ranging from approximately 1.44x to 1.96x\u2014generates a low-to-high band of $186M to $252M, with $219M as the central estimate. The 1.7x assumption reflects observed capital requirements and investor step-up patterns at this financing stage, though specific exit multiples for the transportation subsector remain limited.\n\nKey uncertainties include (1) the absence of narrowly comparable Series C\u2013stage private transactions to validate the multiplier empirically; (2) stage-progression's reliance on historical patterns that may not reflect frontier-tech capital dynamics; and (3) the heterogeneity of the broader eight-company comp set, which spans different transportation verticals and maturity profiles. The range of $186M\u2013$252M is defensible within these constraints, but the analysis would benefit from closer transaction comparables as they emerge.",
