      "narrative": "C12 Quantum Electronics is a Series A quantum computing company that has raised $19.4M to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 11 peers in our analysis universe: 3 public companies (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private firms including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nGiven the nascent stage and heterogeneity of quantum computing development approaches, only one valuation method proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current enterprise value, applied a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to early-stage progression. This yielded an implied valuation of $39M. The peer-median approach could not be deployed; although 8 quantum computing peers exist in the broader dataset, none met the narrow filters for same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier comparables. Constructing a median from the full sector would introduce unacceptable bias given the wide variance in quantum computing architectures and commercialization timelines across peers.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $33M to $45M, with a median point estimate of $39M. Key uncertainties include the lack of tight-stage comparables to ground multiples, heterogeneity in technology approach across the sector, and the pre-revenue or early-revenue status typical of Series A quantum hardware and software firms. This range should be updated as additional same-stage private transactions surface or as C12's own operating metrics materialize.",
