      "narrative": "DiamFab is a seed-stage semiconductor company founded by Khaled Driche, Gauthier Chicot, and Ivan Llaurado, having raised \u20ac8.7M to date. The Chips & Semiconductors sector contains 3 public comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) and 8 private peers including Cerebras, Credo Semiconductor, and SambaNova Systems, though narrowly filtered peer sets proved insufficient for reliable median valuation work.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using the \u20ac8.7M (~$9M) total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next stage yields an implied valuation of $22M. The Peer-Median approach was not feasible due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow semiconductor subset that would meet minimum sample thresholds. Public-Comp Anchoring could not be applied because DiamFab's revenue is not disclosed, a standard constraint for private companies; the public semiconductor sector median trades at 18.9x P/S, but remains inapplicable without target revenue data.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $18M to $25M, centered on $22M. This single-method triangulation carries material uncertainty. Key risk factors include the thinness of seed-stage semiconductor peer data and the absence of revenue disclosure, which precludes revenue-multiple validation. Refinement would require either additional transaction comparables at identical stage or disclosure of DiamFab's near-term revenue trajectory.",
