      "narrative": "Synspective is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised approximately $220M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of five same-sector, same-stage public comparables: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is applicable and yields a median valuation of $7.6B across this five-company set. The range among peers is wide\u2014from $840M to $1.6T\u2014reflecting substantial heterogeneity in scale and market position within the sector. A public-comp anchoring approach using price-to-sales multiples cannot be applied because Synspective's revenue is not on file; the broader Space & Aerospace public sector trades at a median 24.4x revenue across six tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL), but this multiple is not actionable without the target's topline.\n\nThe single triangulation method supports a valuation range of $6.4B to $8.7B, with a midpoint of $7.6B. This analysis carries material uncertainty given the extreme dispersion in comparable valuations and the absence of revenue data to ground multiples-based approaches. The peer set itself spans two orders of magnitude, limiting the precision of any point estimate. Revenue disclosure or transaction-based evidence would materially strengthen conviction in this range.",
