      "narrative": "iQPS is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Tetsuo Yasaka, Akira Sakurai, and Kunihiro Funakoshi. The valuation analysis draws from a peer set of five same-sector, same-stage public companies: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across the five comparables is $7.6B, with valuations ranging from a floor of $840M to a ceiling of $1.6T. This spread reflects meaningful heterogeneity within the public Space & Aerospace sector, driven by differences in scale, launch cadence, and commercial traction. The public-comp anchoring method via price-to-sales multiples (6 tickers, median P/S of 24.4x) cannot be applied, as iQPS revenue is not on file.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6.4B to $8.7B, centered on the peer median of $7.6B. Key uncertainties include iQPS's revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to peers\u2014critical inputs for refined multiples-based valuation. The wide dispersion in the peer set ($840M to $1.6T) also indicates that sector positioning and commercial maturity drive material valuation variance. Without disclosure of iQPS revenue or path to profitability, the peer-median approach remains the primary anchor.",
