      "narrative": "Axelspace is a public-stage Space & Aerospace company. The valuation analysis draws on a peer set of five same-sector, same-stage comparables: SpaceX ($1.6T), Rocket Lab ($40.0B), Planet Labs ($7.6B), Firefly Aerospace ($2.9B), and Astroscale ($840M).\n\nThe peer-median method is the primary applicable triangulation approach. The median valuation across the five comparables is $7.6B, with a range spanning $840M to $1.6T. This wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in company maturity, addressable market, and stage within the public equity phase. The public-comp anchoring method using sector P/S multiples (median 24.4x across six Space & Aerospace tickers) cannot be applied, as Axelspace's revenue is not on file.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6.4B to $8.7B, centered on a $7.6B median. Key uncertainties include Axelspace's actual revenue run-rate and margin profile relative to the peer median, given the substantial dispersion in the peer set. The $1.6T SpaceX valuation and $840M Astroscale valuation anchor opposing ends; Axelspace's positioning within this range depends on disclosed financial performance and market position specificity not present in available data. Single-method triangulation carries inherent sensitivity to peer selection and comparability assumptions.",
