      "narrative": "Terra Drone is a public-stage company in the Drones & Autonomous sector, having completed its IPO on the Tokyo exchange. The valuation exercise confronts a constrained comp universe: while seven private peers operate within Drones & Autonomous\u2014including Waymo, Wayve, Zipline, Joby Aviation, and Nuro\u2014no public comparables exist in this sector. This structural absence of traded peer data materially limits valuation methodology.\n\nThe peer-median approach, which would typically triangulate valuation multiples across same-stage and adjacent-stage competitors, is not applicable here. The screening identified zero same-stage public peers, zero adjacent-stage public peers, and zero similarly-tiered companies meeting the minimum three-datapoint threshold required for statistical reliability. Expanding to all seven private-sector peers would violate disciplined comp selection, as stage heterogeneity and capital structures across this group (ranging from late-stage private to pre-revenue) would render any median multiple misleading rather than instructive.\n\nWithout sufficient public trading data or a sufficiently tight private peer cluster, traditional triangulation methods do not yield a defensible valuation range. The key uncertainty is Terra Drone's specific operational metrics\u2014revenue scale, unit economics, and path to profitability\u2014relative to the known private peer set. A credible valuation would require either: fundamental DCF work anchored to Terra Drone's prospectus disclosure, or serial transaction comparables from recent funding rounds within the Drones & Autonomous space. The current data set supports neither approach.",
