      "narrative": "Digantara is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $50M+ to date. Valuation analysis relies on two applicable methods given the private company's lack of disclosed revenue. The peer universe comprises four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B), alongside five public comparables in Space & Aerospace with a median price-to-sales multiple of 24.4x.\n\nStage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $95M based on the $50M raised proxy. Peer-median valuation across the four private comparables implies $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to the absence of revenue disclosure, a standard limitation in private company analysis.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range spans $81M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $872M. This wide spread reflects material dispersion within the peer set, driven primarily by Sierra Space's outsized $8.0B valuation. Key uncertainties include the absence of revenue and profitability metrics, the heterogeneity of peer business models within space and aerospace, and staging ambiguity across the comparable set. Narrowing this range would require additional disclosure on Digantara's revenue traction and technology differentiation relative to peers.",
