      "narrative": "GalaxEye is a Series A frontier-tech company in Space & Aerospace founded by Suyash Singh and Kishan Thakkar, having raised $10M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, Sierra Space, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-Progression analysis uses the $10M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x multiplier typical of Series A-to-next-stage progression, implying a $20M valuation. Peer-Median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B (Starcloud at seed stage, Aalyria and Cowboy Space at Series B). Public-Comp Anchoring is not applicable: while the Space & Aerospace public sector trades at a 24.4x median P/S across six tickers, GalaxEye's revenue is not on file, precluding revenue multiple application.\n\nThe triangulated range is $17M to $1.5B, with a median of $660M across both methods. This wide dispersion reflects the material stage and maturity gap between stage-progression mechanics and peer trading multiples in a capital-intensive sector. Key uncertainties include revenue traction (unavailable for direct public-comp calibration), customer concentration, and technical de-risking relative to the named private peer set. The peer-median anchor of $1.3B should be weighted with skepticism absent demonstrated revenue or unit economics parity with Series B comparables.",
