      "narrative": "Ocius Technology, a Series B-stage defense and security company, presents a valuation challenge given its unique market positioning within a peer set of eight private comparables and two public defense contractors (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS). The company has secured A$176M in funding, primarily through an Australian Program of Record contract awarded in March 2026.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using the A$176M total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage advancement, yields $334M. Peer-median analysis across eight same-sector, same-stage companies (Dream Security at $3.0B, Allen Control Systems at $2.2B, Harmattan AI at $1.4B, Code Metal at $1.2B, and Twenty at $1.0B) produces a median valuation of $1.1B, with a range spanning $300M to $3.0B. The wide peer dispersion reflects heterogeneity in revenue maturity and contract scale within the defense segment.\n\nTriangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $284M (low) to $1.3B (high), with a median of $730M. Key uncertainties include revenue runway on the Australian contract, international contract expansion likelihood, and whether peer valuations reflect comparable program-of-record revenue stability. The stage-progression method may underweight Ocius's contracted revenue visibility, while peer-median may not fully account for geographic or customer concentration risk specific to the Australian defense market.",
