      "narrative": "QuamCore, a Series A quantum computing company founded by Alon Cohen, is evaluated against a sector peer set of 11 total entities: three public companies (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and eight private firms including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nThe valuation analysis relies on stage-progression methodology, as peer-median triangulation proved inapplicable. The quantum computing private peer universe lacks sufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables meeting narrow filtering criteria\u2014zero same-stage, zero adjacent-stage datapoints emerged from the peer set. Consequently, stage-progression anchors to QuamCore's $35M total capital raised, applying a 2.0x multiplier typical for Series A advancement to subsequent rounds, yielding a $70M implied valuation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $60M to $80M, with a median point of $70M. This relatively narrow band reflects reliance on a single applicable method rather than true triangulation across multiple independent approaches. Key uncertainties include the representativeness of the 2.0x stage step-up multiplier within the quantum computing sector\u2014a domain with heterogeneous capital requirements and development timelines\u2014and the absence of directly comparable Series A-stage quantum firms to validate progression assumptions. Investors should treat the $70M point estimate as indicative pending availability of narrower peer data or alternative valuation signals.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-06T13:29:28+00:00"
