      "narrative": "Qedma is a Series A quantum computing company founded by Asif Sinay, Netanel Lindner, and Dorit Aharonov, having raised $26M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 3 public comps (IONQ, RGTI, QBTS) and 8 private-stage peers including Quantinuum, IonQ, PsiQuantum, D-Wave Quantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nGiven the nascent and heterogeneous nature of the quantum computing market, only one valuation method proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $26M total raised as a proxy for current enterprise value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $52M. Peer-median analysis was not viable due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparable datapoints within the quantum computing peer set\u2014while 8 private peers exist in the sector, none met the narrow filtering criteria required for reliable median extraction.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $44M to $60M, with a median point of $52M. This reflects a single-method triangulation and carries material uncertainty around (1) the relevance of the 2.0x step-up multiplier to an early-stage, capital-intensive hardware company; (2) the absence of directly comparable Series A peers; and (3) broader quantum computing market maturity and funding cycle dynamics. Additional comparables or disclosure of recent secondary transactions would strengthen conviction in this range.",
