      "narrative": "Classiq is a Series C quantum computing software platform that has raised $200M+ to date. The quantum computing sector comprises 11 tracked peers: 3 public companies (IonQ, Rigetti Computing, D-Wave Quantum) and 8 private firms including Quantinuum, PsiQuantum, and SandboxAQ.\n\nA stage-progression methodology is applicable to this valuation. Using total capital raised ($200M) as a proxy for current enterprise value and applying a typical Series C-to-next-stage multiplier of 1.7x yields an implied valuation of $340M. This reflects the step-up in value expected at the late venture stage. A peer-median approach is not executable: while 8 private quantum companies exist in the dataset, none qualify as true comparables within the same funding stage, adjacent stage, or similar valuation tier, falling short of the minimum 3-datapoint threshold for statistical reliability.\n\nThe triangulation produces a median valuation of $340M, with a range between $289M (low) and $391M (high) derived from stage-progression sensitivity analysis. Key uncertainties center on the quantum sector's nascent commercialization timeline, which creates wide dispersion in peer valuations and limits traditional comparable company analysis. The single-method support warrants caution; independent validation through revenue multiple, discounted cash flow, or venture capital method frameworks would strengthen conviction in this range.",
