      "narrative": "Majestic Labs is a Series A-stage semiconductor company that has raised $100M+ to date. The valuation assessment draws on a comparison universe of eight private peers in the Chips & Semiconductors sector\u2014including Rebellions, d-Matrix, and Positron AI at comparable or adjacent stages\u2014alongside three public semiconductor benchmarks (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. The stage-progression method, anchoring to the $100M total raised as a proxy for current valuation, applies a typical 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, implying a valuation of $200M. The peer-median method uses three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables: Rebellions ($2.3B), d-Matrix ($2.0B), and Positron AI ($1.0B). The median across this set is $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied because the target's revenue is not on file, which is standard for private companies at this stage. The public semiconductor sector median trades at 18.9x price-to-sales, but without disclosed revenue, this method is not actionable.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $170M to $2.3B, with a median of $1.1B across the two applicable methods. The wide range reflects material uncertainty: the stage-progression method yields a substantially lower result than peer medians, suggesting either that comparable firms commanded premium valuations at Series A or that Majestic Labs' capital efficiency or market position differs meaningfully from peers. Revenue visibility and technical differentiation remain the primary value drivers that would narrow this band.",
