      "narrative": "Speedata is a Series B semiconductor company founded by Jonathan Friedmann and five co-founders that has raised $114M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 8 private and 3 public semiconductor firms, including same-stage peers like Positron AI and adjacent-stage players including Rebellions, d-Matrix, and DEEPX.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $217M. Peer-median anchoring across four same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (Rebellions at $2.3B, d-Matrix at $2.0B, Positron AI at $1.0B, DEEPX at $529M) produces a $1.5B median valuation, with a range spanning $529M to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring via the three semiconductor public tickers (ALAB, NVDA, AMD) cannot be applied; while the sector P/S median is 18.9x, Speedata's revenue is not disclosed, precluding a meaningful revenue multiple application.\n\nThe two applicable methods triangulate to a range of $184M (low) to $1.7B (high), with a median of $858M. The wide dispersion reflects meaningful uncertainty around whether Speedata tracks closer to early-stage private comps or to more mature Series B comparables like Positron AI. Revenue visibility, customer concentration, and product commercialization timeline remain critical value drivers not fully captured in stage-based metrics alone.",
