      "narrative": "NordSpace, a Series A space and aerospace company founded by Rahul Goel with $38M+ raised to date, is valued within a universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods triangulate a defensible range. Stage-progression applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier to the $38M total raised proxy, implying $76M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation ($2.0B Series B), Aalyria ($1.3B Series B), and Starcloud ($1.1B Seed)\u2014yields a median of $1.3B with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. Public-comp anchoring is inapplicable; the sector median P/S across public Space & Aerospace names is 24.4x, but NordSpace's revenue is not disclosed. \n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $65M (low) to $1.5B (high), with a median of $688M. This wide dispersion reflects stage uncertainty: the stage-progression method yields a conservative floor based on capital deployed, while peer-median incorporates later-stage, higher-valuation comparable transactions. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, competitive positioning relative to named peers, and path to Series B pricing. Further financial disclosure or milestone achievement would narrow this range materially.",
