      "narrative": "Stratek Global is a growth-stage nuclear energy company founded by Kelvin Kemm. The valuation analysis draws from a sector universe of 11 peers: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms, including Helion, Oklo, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Nano Nuclear Energy.\n\nStandard peer-median triangulation is not applicable here. The nuclear energy sector contains only 6 same-sector comparables, but filtering by stage alignment, adjacent-stage proximity, or valuation tier yields fewer than three datapoints in any single cohort\u2014the minimum threshold required for meaningful median analysis. A cross-sector median would introduce material distortion given nuclear energy's distinct capital intensity, regulatory profile, and commercialization timelines relative to broader technology markets.\n\nConsequently, this analysis cannot support a single quantitative valuation range based on the available data. A defensible valuation would require either: (1) expansion of the private peer dataset with stage-aligned, non-public transactions; (2) direct cost-of-capital modeling anchored to company-specific capex and cash-flow projections; or (3) precedent transaction analysis within nuclear energy subsectors. The key uncertainty remains the sparse liquidity and transaction history in growth-stage nuclear ventures, which limits benchmark reliability. Further diligence on comparable funding rounds or strategic acquisition multiples in this sector would be necessary to narrow valuation bounds.",
