      "narrative": "Terrahaptix, a seed-stage defense and security company founded by Nathan Nwachukwu and Maxwell Maduka, has raised $52M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private companies and 2 public peers in the Defense & Security sector, including seed and Series A stage companies.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $52M total raised as a proxy for current value, applying a typical seed-to-next-stage multiplier of 2.5x, yielding $130M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014UFORCE ($1.0B, Seed), Singularity ($400M, Series A), and NODA AI ($125M, Series A)\u2014establishes a median of $400M, with a range of $125M to $1.0B.\n\nTriangulation of these two methods supports a valuation range of $110M (low) to $460M (high), with a median of $265M. The wide range reflects material uncertainty inherent in seed-stage valuation: the peer-median method is heavily influenced by UFORCE's $1.0B valuation, which may not reflect Terrahaptix's current stage maturity or traction. Stage-progression, conversely, assumes near-term capital deployment and retention of raised capital value. Key uncertainties include customer traction metrics, technology differentiation relative to the peer set, and momentum toward Series A close. Further diligence on revenue, customer concentration, and product-market validation would narrow this range.",
