      "narrative": "OroraTech is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised \u20ac38M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 4 private peers at Series B/C stages (Sierra Space, Cowboy Space Corporation, Aalyria, Skyryse) and 5 public aerospace comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL).\n\nTwo valuation methods were applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the \u20ac38M raised as a proxy base value and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, implies a valuation of \u20ac72M. Peer-median analysis across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private comparables yields a median valuation of \u20ac1.6B, with a range spanning \u20ac1.1B to \u20ac8.0B. Public-comp anchoring could not be applied due to the absence of revenue data. The public sector median trade at 24.4x price-to-sales, but this multiple cannot be applied without OroraTech's disclosed revenue.\n\nThe triangulation of applicable methods supports a valuation range of \u20ac61M (low) to \u20ac1.9B (high), with a median of \u20ac861M. The wide dispersion reflects material stage and scale heterogeneity within the peer set; Sierra Space's \u20ac8B Series C valuation is a significant outlier. Key uncertainties include OroraTech's revenue trajectory, unit economics, and whether near-term funding will shift the company into the higher-valuation cohort occupied by Cowboy Space and Aalyria.",
