      "narrative": "Atmos Space Cargo is a Series A space and aerospace cargo company that has raised \u20ac30M to date. The valuation assessment draws on a peer universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers across the space sector, including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs at various stages.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the \u20ac30M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A-to-subsequent-stage progression, implying a valuation of \u20ac60M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector companies at Series B or adjacent stages\u2014Cowboy Space Corporation (\u20ac2.0B), Aalyria (\u20ac1.3B), and Starcloud (\u20ac1.1B)\u2014yielding a median valuation of \u20ac1.3B. Public-comp anchoring via P/S multiples (median 24.4x across the 5 public tickers) cannot be applied because target revenue is not disclosed.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range is \u20ac51M (low) to \u20ac1.5B (high), with a median of \u20ac680M. This wide dispersion reflects structural uncertainty: the stage-progression method produces a conservative floor, while peer-median analysis implies substantially higher valuations driven by comparables at later stages. Key uncertainties include whether Atmos will achieve comparable traction to Series B peers, and the appropriate stage discount from late-stage benchmarks to current-stage reality.",
