      "narrative": "Orbem is a Series B biotech company that has raised \u20ac55.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of three public peers (RXRX, TEM, ONT.L) and eight private-stage biotech companies, including Series C-stage comparables Colossal Biosciences, Chai Discovery, and New Limit.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses total capital raised (\u20ac55.5M) as a proxy for current value and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical for Series B advancement, yielding \u20ac105M. Peer-median analysis draws on three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies with a median valuation of \u20ac3.8B (range: \u20ac3.1B\u2013\u20ac10.3B). Public-comp anchoring via price-to-sales multiples cannot be applied due to the absence of revenue disclosure, which is standard for private-stage companies. The peer median of 8.1x across the three public tickers is noted for context but not operationalized.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of \u20ac90M (low) to \u20ac4.4B (high), with a median of \u20ac2.0B. This wide range reflects material uncertainty inherent in early-stage biotech valuations: the stage-progression method implies modest value relative to capital invested, while peer multiples suggest significantly higher valuations if Orbem demonstrates comparable technical or commercial progress to Series C peers. Key uncertainties include asset maturity, clinical/technical validation progress, and whether peer comparables are truly representative of Orbem's risk profile.",
