      "narrative": "Calogena, a Series A nuclear energy company founded by Julien Dereux, has raised \u20ac100M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of 11 peers spanning public and private markets: 3 public companies (OKLO, NNE, SMR) and 8 private firms including Fuse Energy, Helion, Valar Atomics, X-Energy, and Oklo, representing the same sector and adjacent development stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression uses the \u20ac100M raised as a proxy base value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A progression, implying a $200M valuation. Peer-median analysis across 3 same-sector comparables\u2014Valar Atomics (Series B, $6.0B), Nano Nuclear Energy (Seed, $808M), and Fuse Energy (Series A, $200M)\u2014yields a median valuation of $808M, with a range of $200M to $6.0B.\n\nThe two methods triangulate to a valuation range of $170M to $929M, with a median of $504M. This wide spread reflects material stage and maturity variance within the peer set; the $6.0B outlier (Valar Atomics at Series B) and early-stage comparables at $200M\u2013$808M create substantial uncertainty. Key risks to valuation include execution on commercialization timelines, regulatory pathway clarity, and capital intensity of nuclear deployment. A Series A valuation in the $200M\u2013$600M range appears defensible given Fuse Energy precedent and sector comparable volatility.",
