      "narrative": "Credo Semiconductor is a public-stage company in Chips & Semiconductors that went public via IPO in 2022. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 3 public peers in the same sector and stage: Cerebras ($39.2B), Ouster ($2.3B), and Aeva Technologies ($1.1B).\n\nThe peer-median method is the applicable triangulation approach here. The median valuation across these 3 same-sector, same-stage comparables is $2.3B, with a range spanning $1.1B at the low end to $39.2B at the high end. This wide dispersion reflects material heterogeneity in the semiconductor frontier-tech space, where valuations diverge sharply based on technology differentiation and commercialization trajectory. A public-comp anchoring approach using price-to-sales multiples\u2014with a median P/S of 18.9x observed across ALAB, NVDA, and AMD\u2014cannot be applied due to the absence of Credo's revenue figures in the dataset.\n\nBased on the peer-median method alone, the analysis supports a valuation range of $1.9B to $2.6B, with a median of $2.3B. The key uncertainty is the limited methodological foundation: only one applicable triangulation method constrains the estimate. The wide valuation range across the peer set ($1.1B to $39.2B) underscores substantial market ambiguity around frontier-chip companies' near-term revenue trajectories and technology adoption risk. Additional revenue or profitability data would materially strengthen conviction in this range.",
