      "narrative": "Portal Space Systems, a Series A-stage space & aerospace company founded by Jeff Thornburg, Ian Vorbach, and Prashaanth Ravindran, has raised $62.85M to date. Valuation is triangulated across a universe of 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including SpaceX, Rocket Lab, and Planet Labs.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression anchors to the $62.85M raised as a proxy for current value and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A advancement, yielding $126M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage private companies (Cowboy Space at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Starcloud at $1.1B) produces a median valuation of $1.3B. Public-comp anchoring using a 24.4x sector P/S median across the five public tickers is not applicable due to the absence of disclosed revenue for Portal.\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $107M to $1.5B, with a median of $713M. This wide band reflects material tension between stage-relative and peer-cohort methods. Key uncertainties include Portal's current revenue run rate, customer traction relative to the peer set, and stage classification\u2014adjacent-stage positioning materially shifts the applicable peer median. Additional operational metrics on burn rate and runway would refine the stage-progression multiplier.",
