      "narrative": "Mitra Chem, a Series B climate and energy company founded by Vivas Kumar and Will Chueh, has raised $60M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine private companies and one public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA) operating in the same sector and stage cohort.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression methodology uses the $60M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $114M. Peer-median analysis examined three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage companies: KoBold Metals ($3.0B Series C), Electric Hydrogen ($1.0B Series C), and Amogy ($700M Series C). The median of this peer set is $1.0B, with a range of $700M to $3.0B. These two methods are both applicable given the availability of stage-comparable and sector-comparable transactions.\n\nThe triangulation across both methods supports a valuation range of $97M (low) to $1.1B (high), with a median implied value of $557M. The wide spread reflects material uncertainty around whether Mitra Chem's development stage, technology maturity, and capital efficiency align more closely with the earlier stage-progression baseline or the higher peer median. Key uncertainties include commercialization timeline, capital requirements to scale, and competitive positioning relative to the three peer reference points.",
