      "narrative": "Looking Glass, a Series A semiconductor company founded by Shawn Frayne, has raised $30M to date. The valuation analysis triangulates across a peer set of 3 private companies in Chips & Semiconductors at the same or adjacent stage (Rebellions at $2.3B Series A, d-Matrix at $2.0B Series A, Positron AI at $1.0B Series B) alongside 3 public semiconductor comparables (ALAB, NVDA, AMD).\n\nTwo valuation methods apply. Stage-progression anchors to the $30M raised as a proxy for post-money valuation, applying a typical 2.0x multiplier for advancement to the next stage, implying $60M. Peer-median directly references the 3-company cohort, which trades at a $1.0B median with a range of $1.0B to $2.3B. Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of revenue data; the sector median P/S of 18.9x cannot be meaningfully deployed without target financials.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $51M (floor) to $2.3B (ceiling), with a median of $1.0B across both applicable methods. The wide dispersion reflects material uncertainty: stage-progression suggests early-stage pricing near $60M, while peer comps\u2014especially Rebellions' $2.3B valuation\u2014indicate significant stretch multiples are achievable in the current frontier-chip financing environment. Key unknowns include Looking Glass's technical differentiation relative to peers and the timing and certainty of revenue inflection. The median estimate of $1.0B balances these tensions but should be weighted against the stage-progression floor absent clear technical or market validation.",
