      "narrative": "Cambium is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Simon Waddington and Stephan Herrera that has raised $127M+ to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014operating in the same sector and stage, including Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Divergent, and Exotec.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for post-money valuation, applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding an implied value of $241M. Peer-median analysis across three directly comparable Series B robotics companies\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B)\u2014produces a median valuation of $1.8B with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce materially different signals. The stage-progression approach suggests $241M; the peer-median approach indicates $1.8B. A triangulated range spanning both methods yields a low of $205M, median of $996M, and high of $2.0B. The wide dispersion reflects two core uncertainties: whether Cambium's operational metrics and growth trajectory align with higher-valued peer cohorts, and whether the stage-progression method\u2014which anchors to historical capital deployed\u2014adequately captures recent market pricing in frontier robotics. Resolution requires detail on revenue run-rate, unit economics, and competitive positioning relative to named peers.",
