      "narrative": "Wispr AI is a Series A-stage artificial intelligence and software company founded by Tanay Kothari and Sahaj Garg that has raised $81.6M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of nine private frontier-tech firms and one public comparable (Palantir), with primary focus on four same-sector peers at Series A or Series B stage: Reflection AI ($25.0B), Physical Intelligence ($5.6B), Black Forest Labs ($3.2B), and Field AI ($2.0B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total raised as a proxy for current valuation and applying a standard 2.0x Series A step-up multiplier, yields $163M. Peer-median analysis across the four comparables produces a median valuation of $4.4B, with a range spanning $2.0B to $25.0B. The peer set exhibits substantial dispersion, reflecting varying technology maturity and commercial traction within the frontier-AI segment.\n\nSynthesizing both methods produces a triangulated valuation range of $139M (low) to $5.1B (high), with a median of $2.3B. The wide spread reflects two distinct considerations: stage-progression suggests Wispr commands a modest premium to capital deployed, while peer benchmarking suggests substantially higher valuations are defensible within the sector. Key uncertainties center on comparative product differentiation, revenue traction relative to stage peers, and whether capital raised adequately reflects risk-adjusted enterprise value or represents downround dynamics in a selective market.",
