      "narrative": "Sierra Space, a Series C space and aerospace company founded by Fatih and Eren Ozmen, carries a current post-money valuation of $8.0B against $2.0B in total capital raised. The valuation was triangulated against a comp universe spanning 5 public tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers across the space and aerospace sector, including Impulse Space ($4.3B, Series D), Apex Space ($2.3B, Series D), and Varda Space Industries ($1.6B, Series D).\n\nTwo methods proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, applying a 1.7x multiplier to the $8.0B base valuation to reflect Series C to next-stage advancement, implies $13.6B. Peer-median analysis across six same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yielded a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range spanning $1.1B to $4.3B. Public-comp anchoring was not applied due to the absence of disclosed revenue figures for the target.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range spans $1.5B (low) to $15.6B (high), with a median of $7.7B. This wide spread reflects material tension between stage-progression methodology, which anchors to the existing $8.0B round, and peer-median analysis, which suggests substantially lower valuations. Key uncertainties include revenue scale and growth trajectory relative to listed peers, as well as execution risk typical to Series C capital intensity in aerospace.",
