      "narrative": "CesiumAstro is a Series C-stage Space & Aerospace company that has raised $470M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of 7 private peers in the same sector and stage, supplemented by 5 public Space & Aerospace companies (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) for sector benchmarking context.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, yielding $799M. Peer-median valuation across 7 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage peers\u2014including Sierra Space ($8.0B), Impulse Space ($4.3B), Apex Space ($2.3B), and others\u2014produces a median of $2.0B, with a range of $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comparable anchoring cannot be applied due to absence of target revenue data, standard for private companies.\n\nTriangulation of the two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $679M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.4B. The wide range reflects material dispersion in peer valuations and stage-progression conservatism relative to median peer positioning. Key uncertainties include revenue trajectory, customer concentration, and technical execution risk\u2014typical valuation drivers in early-stage aerospace ventures where public comparables trade at 24.4x median price-to-sales.",
