      "narrative": "Loft Orbital is a Series C-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $326M to date. Valuation analysis triangulates across a peer universe of 13 comparable companies\u20145 public (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private firms in the same sector and adjacent funding stages, including Sierra Space, Impulse Space, Apex Space, and Varda Space Industries.\n\nTwo methodologies proved applicable. Stage-progression analysis, using the $326M total raised as a proxy base and applying a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, implies a valuation of $554M. Peer-median analysis across 7 same-sector comparables yields a median valuation of $2.0B, with a range spanning $1.15B to $8.0B. Public-comp anchoring via Space & Aerospace P/S multiples (median 24.4x across 6 tickers) cannot be applied absent disclosed revenue figures. \n\nTriangulating these two applicable methods produces a valuation range of $471M (low) to $2.3B (high), with a median of $1.3B. The wide band reflects material dispersion in peer valuations and stage maturity across the comparable set. Key uncertainties include capital deployment trajectory relative to revenue generation, competitive positioning versus higher-valued peers like Sierra Space ($8.0B), and whether current market conditions for aerospace funding persist.",
