      "narrative": "Compound Eye is a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Jason Devitt and Haoyang Wang that has raised $20.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of nine private frontier-tech companies in robotics and manufacturing, supplemented by one public market reference point.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $20.6M total raised as a proxy anchor and applies a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B advancement, implying a valuation of $39M. Peer-median analysis examines three same-sector, same-stage comparables: Generalist AI ($2.0B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B), and Dexterity ($1.6B). The median of this peer set is $1.8B, with a range of $1.6B to $2.0B. The stage-progression method is mechanically sound but reflects capital efficiency; the peer method captures market pricing for similar risk-stage companies but exhibits wide dispersion typical of frontier robotics.\n\nThe two methods produce valuations spanning $39M to $1.8B. A defensible estimate ranges from $33M (low) to $2.0B (high), with a median of $895M. Material uncertainty reflects the sector's valuation volatility and the absence of recent comparable financings at Compound Eye's specific revenue or technical maturity stage. Resolution of this range requires clarity on revenue traction and technical differentiation relative to the named peer set.",
