      "narrative": "Viken Detection is a Series C-stage defense and security company that has raised $50M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparables universe of 10 peers (2 public, 8 private), including same-stage companies Castelion ($13.0B), Stark Defence ($4.0B), and Neros ($2.5B).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a valuation proxy, applied a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical for Series C advancement, yielding $85M. Peer-median analysis across three same-sector, same-stage comparables produced a median valuation of $4.0B, with a range spanning $2.5B to $13.0B. The wide peer range reflects material variance in market positioning and investor appetite within the defense tech subsector.\n\nTriangulating these methods produces a valuation range of $72M (low) to $4.6B (high), with a median of $2.0B. The significant spread between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects tension between Viken's modest capital deployment relative to peer funding, and the substantially higher valuations commanded by comparably-staged defense companies. Key uncertainties include customer concentration, regulatory approval timelines, and whether Viken's technology differentiation justifies a position toward the peer range upper or lower bound. Resolution of these factors is critical to narrowing the $4.5B spread.",
      "lastUpdated": "2026-09-06T13:41:58+00:00"
