      "narrative": "Citra Space Corporation is a Series A-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $15M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of 3 private peers at Series A/B stages (Cowboy Space, Aalyria, Starcloud) and 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) spanning the broader Space & Aerospace sector.\n\nTwo triangulation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier from the $15M raised as a proxy base, implying a $30M valuation. Peer-median analysis across the 3 private comparables yields a median valuation of $1.3B, with a range of $1.1B to $2.0B. The public-comp anchoring method cannot be applied due to absence of revenue data for the target. The triangulated range spans $26M (low, stage-progression floor) to $1.5B (high, upper peer quartile), with a median of $665M.\n\nThe wide dispersion between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects structural uncertainty: the stage-progression method is mechanical and conservative, while peer comparables may overweight later-stage or more mature entrants. Public P/S multiples in the sector average 24.4x but cannot inform this analysis without target revenue visibility. The $665M median should be treated as indicating relative positioning within the peer set rather than a point estimate; key uncertainties include capital efficiency trajectory, customer traction, and technical de-risking milestones typical for Series A advancement.",
