      "narrative": "Orbital Inc. is a Seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Euwyn Poon that has raised an undisclosed amount through a16z Speedrun. The valuation analysis is constrained by a limited peer universe: while 14 same-sector private companies exist, only 1 operates at the same stage, and the public comp set comprises 5 traded Space & Aerospace firms (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) with a median price-to-sales multiple of 24.4x.\n\nOf three valuation methods tested, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using a $16M proxy for total raised and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage progression, the method implies a $40M valuation. The Peer-Median approach failed due to insufficient granular comparables at the same stage and valuation tier; the Public-Comp Anchoring method could not be applied because Orbital's revenue is not disclosed, a common constraint for private companies.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $34M to $46M, with a median point of $40M. This range reflects the Stage-Progression output and conservative adjustments for single-method reliance. Key uncertainties include the precision of the total-raised proxy, the applicability of 2.5x multipliers to frontier-tech capital structures, and the absence of same-stage private comparables to validate peer-driven benchmarks. Revenue disclosure would enable public-multiple triangulation and tighten the range materially.",
