      "narrative": "Govini is a Growth-stage defense and security software company that has raised $174M to date. The broader Defense & Security sector encompasses 10 comparable companies across public and private markets\u20142 public-traded entities (DRSHF, IDEAFORGE.NS) and 8 private peers including Anduril Industries, Helsing, and Shield AI\u2014though the immediate peer set at Govini's stage and valuation tier is limited.\n\nGiven sparse same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables, the Peer-Median method was not applicable; no sufficiently narrow cohort of three or more direct peers could be isolated to support a reliable multiple-based valuation. Consequently, valuation relies on Stage-Progression analysis, which applies a 1.2x step-up multiplier to the $174M capital raised proxy, implying a value of $209M. This methodology reflects typical Growth-stage repricing dynamics absent transaction data for direct peers.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $177M to $240M, with a median of $209M. The lower bound reflects downside conservatism on capital-raised anchoring; the upper bound incorporates sector positioning and capital intensity. Key uncertainties include the absence of recent transaction comparables in the immediate Defense & Security peer set at this stage and valuation tier, limiting precision. Revenue multiples, profitability metrics, and customer concentration data would significantly narrow this range but were not available for this analysis.",
