      "narrative": "Nth Cycle is a Growth-stage climate and energy company founded by Megan O'Connor and Chad Vecitis, having raised $60M in equity alongside a $1.1B 10-year offtake agreement with Trafigura. The Climate & Energy sector comprises a sparse comp universe of 1 public company (LNZA) and 8 private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix.\n\nTraditional peer-median valuation proved inapplicable here. A systematic screen across same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar-valuation-tier subsets yielded fewer than three datapoints in each category, falling below the minimum threshold for reliable multiples analysis. While 8 same-sector private peers exist, none satisfied stage and tier alignment criteria simultaneously. An all-sector median approach would introduce unacceptable noise given the heterogeneity of climate tech business models, capital intensity, and commercialization timelines.\n\nThe lack of comparable trading multiples or recent private funding rounds at similar scale and stage limits conventional triangulation methods. Any valuation framework here must rely heavily on the $1.1B Trafigura offtake agreement as a binding commercial signal, though translating an offtake contract into enterprise value requires explicit assumptions about margin, duration, and financial leverage that fall outside the data provided. A rigorous estimate demands either (1) stage-specific venture return thresholds, or (2) DCF analysis anchored to the offtake terms\u2014neither of which can be derived from peer comparables alone. Key uncertainty remains the conversion of long-term contracted revenue into present-value equity worth given the capital-intensive nature of scale-up in this sector.",
