      "narrative": "MATERIAL operates in the Climate & Energy sector at Seed stage, having raised $7.1M plus $1.25M in USAF SBIR funding. The company's comp universe includes one public comparable (Linamar, ticker LNZA) and eight private peers in the climate tech space, including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix.\n\nStage-progression analysis is the primary applicable valuation method. Using total capital raised of $7M as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next stage yields an implied valuation of $18M. A peer-median approach could not be applied due to insufficient same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables within the narrow Climate & Energy filter; while eight sector peers exist broadly, fewer than three datapoints met stage and valuation-tier criteria necessary for reliable triangulation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $15M to $20M, with a median of $18M. This range reflects the 2.5x progression assumption applied to the $7M raised base. Key uncertainties include the company's actual pre-money and post-money dynamics across its funding rounds, the relevance of broader Climate & Energy comps given the specialized nature of 3D-printed battery and advanced materials engineering, and the timing and terms of anticipated Series A. Additional founder pedigree (Mercedes-AMG Petronas F1, Rivian, Duke PhD) and USAF validation support downside protection, though quantification of these factors requires forward-looking operational milestones.",
