      "narrative": "Halter is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $420M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparison universe of nine private peers and one public comparable across the robotics and manufacturing sector, including companies such as Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Hadrian at largely contemporaneous or adjacent stages.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, which applies a 1.7x step-up multiplier typical of Series C advancement to the $420M total raised as a proxy baseline, implies a valuation of $714M. Peer-median analysis across seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables yields a median valuation of $1.6B, with a range spanning $1.0B to $2.0B. The peer set includes both Series B and Series D companies, reflecting stage heterogeneity within the robotics cohort.\n\nTriangulating both methods produces a valuation range of $607M to $1.9B, with a median of $1.2B. The material spread reflects uncertainty in appropriate peer comparability and stage-to-stage growth expectations within a sector experiencing significant capital deployment. The peer-median method pulls the range toward the higher end, suggesting market-derived valuations for robotics companies currently exceed simple capital-progression models. Key uncertainties include revenue and unit economics visibility, competitive positioning relative to named peers, and market timing within an evolving sector.",
