      "narrative": "Loyal is a Series C biotech company that has raised $250M+ to date. Valuation analysis relies on a peer set of three same-stage, same-sector comparables in Biotech & Health: Colossal Biosciences ($10.3B), Chai Discovery ($3.8B), and New Limit ($3.1B). Public-market anchoring is not applicable given the absence of disclosed revenue figures.\n\nTwo triangulation methods yield defensible results. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline and applying a typical 1.7x step-up multiplier from Series C onward, implies a valuation of $425M. Peer-median anchoring across the three identified comparables yields $3.8B, reflecting the sector median valuation at this stage. The peer range spans $3.1B to $10.3B, indicating material dispersion in this cohort.\n\nThe two-method triangulation supports a range of $361M to $4.4B, with a median of $2.1B. The wide span reflects genuine uncertainty: stage-progression suggests a conservative floor tied to historical capital deployment, while peer medians embed market assessments of later-stage biotech risk and probability of value realization. Key uncertainties include Loyal's differentiation within the peer set, clinical/regulatory progress since capital raise, and the sustainability of current-market biotech valuations. A point estimate within $1.5B\u2013$3.0B would be most consistent with the stage and median peer positioning.",
