      "narrative": "Somos is a Series B-stage housing and construction company that has raised $105.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comp universe of four private peers in the housing and construction sector\u2014Plantd Materials, Cuby Technologies, Cover, and Charge Robotics\u2014given the absence of direct public comparables in this frontier segment.\n\nThe stage-progression method is the applicable triangulation approach here. Using total capital raised ($106M) as a proxy baseline and applying a 1.9x step-up multiplier typical of Series B-to-next-stage progression, the analysis yields an implied valuation of $201M. This represents the median point in the range and reflects normalized expectation for capital efficiency and growth trajectory at this funding stage.\n\nThe full triangulated range spans $171M (low) to $231M (median: $201M), centered on the stage-progression output. The relatively narrow band reflects reliance on a single methodological lens. Key uncertainties include the appropriateness of the 1.9x step-up multiplier absent more granular comp margin and growth-rate data, the stability of private peer valuations as recent reference points, and the degree to which construction-tech fundamentals have shifted post-Series B for this cohort. The analysis is most robust as a stage-based benchmark rather than a market-based valuation anchor.",
