      "narrative": "EarthGrid is a Seed-stage transportation company that has raised $105.3M to date. The valuation comp universe consists of six private frontier-transport companies including Rivian, The Boring Company, Einride, Navier, and Olympian Motors; no public comparables exist in this nascent segment.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the applicable triangulation approach. Using total capital raised ($105M) as a proxy for implied post-Seed valuation and applying a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-Series A transitions yields $263M. This method grounds the analysis in the company's demonstrated capital absorption and historical stage-progression patterns observed across early-stage transportation ventures.\n\nPeer-median comparison is not applicable due to insufficient narrow peer coverage. While three Transportation-sector companies exist in the available comp set, none meet same-stage, adjacent-stage, or similar-valuation-tier filters required for reliable median derivation. A broader all-sector median would introduce excessive methodological noise.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $224M (low) to $303M (median) with central estimate at $263M. This range reflects \u00b115% variance around the stage-progression point estimate, accounting for execution risk and limited comparables. Key uncertainties include path to Series A fundraising success, actual capital efficiency relative to peer benchmarks, and the durability of frontier-transportation investor appetite. The single-method foundation warrants heightened sensitivity to stage-progression multiplier assumptions.",
