      "narrative": "Axion, a Series B robotics and manufacturing company founded by Daniel First and Rebecca Trachtenberg, has raised $62.1M to date. Valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of nine private firms and one public company (ticker 277810.KQ) operating in the robotics and manufacturing sector at similar or proximate stages. Key private comparables include Generalist AI, Bedrock Robotics, and Dexterity, all Series B stage.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using $62M total raised as a proxy for current value and applying a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B-to-later-stage step-ups, implies $118M. Peer-median capitalization across three same-sector, same-stage comparables (Generalist AI at $2.0B, Bedrock Robotics at $1.8B, and Dexterity at $1.6B) yields a median valuation of $1.8B, with a range of $1.6B\u2013$2.0B.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide implied range of $100M to $2.0B, with a median estimate of $934M. This divergence reflects structural tension between Axion's early capital deployment ($62M) and the markedly higher valuations observed in the peer set. Key uncertainties include whether peer comparables accurately reflect Axion's technology maturity, revenue traction, and addressable market position within robotics and manufacturing. Further diligence on unit economics and customer concentration is warranted to narrow this range.",
