      "narrative": "ASI is a Series B-stage space and aerospace company that has raised $56.1M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 4 private peers at Series B/C stage (Sierra Space at $8.0B, Cowboy Space Corporation at $2.0B, Aalyria at $1.3B, and Skyryse at $1.1B), as well as 5 public space and aerospace tickers with a median P/S multiple of 24.4x.\n\nTwo valuation methods prove applicable. Stage-progression analysis uses the $56.1M total raised as a proxy baseline and applies a 1.9x multiplier typical of Series B advancement, yielding $107M. The peer-median approach anchors to the $1.6B median valuation across the 4 same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (ranging $1.1B to $8.0B). Public-comp anchoring cannot be applied absent revenue disclosure for ASI. The wide dispersion in private peer valuations\u2014driven largely by Sierra Space's $8.0B outlier position\u2014creates substantial range uncertainty.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across these two methods supports a valuation range of $91M (floor, stage-progression) to $1.9B (ceiling, peer-max influence), with a median implied value of $878M. The key uncertainty lies in ASI's position within the peer band: peers span three orders of magnitude, and limited visibility into ASI's revenue, customer traction, and technology differentiation makes placement within that band highly contingent. Further diligence on revenue scale and market positioning would be necessary to narrow the range materially.",
