      "narrative": "Vantage Robotics is a Series C\u2013stage defense and security robotics company founded by Tobin Fisher and Joe van Niekerk that has raised $45.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of three same-stage, same-sector private peers (Castelion at $13.0B, Stark Defence at $4.0B, and Neros at $2.5B), supplemented by a broader set of ten private and two public defense-tech companies including Anduril Industries and Helsing.\n\nTwo valuation methods are applicable. Stage-progression analysis applies a 1.7x multiplier to total capital raised as a proxy base, implying $78M. Peer-median analysis across the three direct comparables yields $4.0B, with a range spanning $2.5B to $13.0B. The wide range reflects heterogeneity in the peer set; Castelion trades at a substantial premium while Neros and Stark Defence cluster more tightly.\n\nTriangulation across both methods produces a low bound of $66M (stage-progression floor), a median of $2.0B, and a high of $4.6B (capped by peer median plus observed dispersion). The sharp divergence between stage-progression and peer-median results reflects material uncertainty around the company's competitive positioning, technology maturity, and revenue scale relative to the comparables set. Near-term revenue visibility, customer concentration, and technical differentiation remain critical value drivers requiring further diligence.",
