      "narrative": "Burro is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $44.8M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a peer universe of 9 comparable companies\u20141 public and 8 private\u2014operating in the same sector and stage band, including Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Hadrian.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis uses the $45M total raised as a proxy base value and applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C-to-next-stage step-ups, implying a $76M valuation. Peer-median analysis examines 7 same-sector comparables spanning Series B and D, which have a median post-money valuation of $1.6B, with a range of $1.0B to $2.0B. This method implies $1.6B for Burro.\n\nThe two methods produce a wide but meaningful range: the stage-progression method yields $76M (low end), while peer median suggests $1.6B (midpoint), with the peer range extending to $1.9B. The median across both methods is $863M. Key uncertainties include revenue run-rate and unit economics relative to peers, stage and maturity positioning versus the heterogeneous Series B-to-D peer set, and the relevance of public-market comparables given the small sample. The $65M\u2013$1.9B range reflects material dispersion; narrowing it requires clarity on Burro's traction trajectory and competitive positioning within its peer cohort.",
