      "narrative": "Tutor Intelligence is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Alon Kosowsky-Sachs and Josh Gruenstein that has raised $42.5M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a comparable universe of 9 private and 1 public company operating in the same sector and stage cohort, including peers such as Humanoid, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, Generalist AI, and Walden Robotics.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy for current value, applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to next-stage advancement, yielding $85M. Peer-median analysis examines five comparable companies across Series A and adjacent stages; the median valuation across this set is $1.6B, with a range from $1.1B (Walden Robotics, Seed) to $2.0B (Generalist AI, Series B).\n\nThe triangulated analysis supports a valuation range of $72M to $1.9B, with a median of $868M. The wide band reflects material tension between the stage-progression method\u2014which anchors to capital deployed\u2014and peer comparables, which span a broader stage range and suggest significantly higher market valuations for robotics companies. Key uncertainties include the appropriate stage adjustment for peers in Series B relative to Tutor Intelligence's Series A position, and whether peer valuations reflect genuine comparability in product maturity, unit economics, or market traction rather than sector-wide valuation expansion.",
