      "narrative": "Verne is a seed-stage climate and energy company that has raised $17.5M to date. The valuation landscape for frontier-tech companies in this sector remains sparse; while eight private climate-tech peers exist alongside one public comparable (Lienzo, ticker LNZA), the absence of same-stage or adjacent-stage peer datapoints prevents meaningful peer-median triangulation. Top private peers include Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix, though these span disparate stages and business models.\n\nThe single applicable valuation method\u2014stage-progression\u2014applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the $17.5M total raised, treated as a proxy for current implied valuation. This yields $43.75M, anchoring the central estimate. Around this median, a plausible range of $37M to $50M captures near-term valuation scenarios, corresponding to approximately 2.1x to 2.9x the capital deployed to date.\n\nThe analysis is constrained by methodological limitations. The absence of sufficiently similar seed-stage comparables means this valuation rests entirely on stage-progression mechanics rather than market-derived multiples. Critical uncertainties include capital efficiency relative to frontier-climate peer cohorts, pathway to next-stage funding, and whether the 2.5x multiplier appropriately reflects current seed-to-Series A conditions in deep-tech. Additional market data or disclosed metrics on burn and runway would materially strengthen conviction in any point estimate.",
