      "narrative": "Aon3D is a Series C robotics and manufacturing company that has raised $14.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws on a peer universe of nine comparable companies\u2014eight private firms and one public entity\u2014operating in the robotics and manufacturing sector at similar or adjacent funding stages. Key private peers include Exotec, Bedrock Robotics, Dexterity, and Hadrian.\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. Stage-progression analysis, using total capital raised as a proxy baseline, applies a 1.7x multiplier typical of Series C advancement, implying a $24M valuation. Peer-median analysis leverages a cohort of seven same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables with valuations ranging from $1.0B to $2.0B and a median of $1.6B, directly implying $1.6B.\n\nThe triangulated range spans $21M (low) to $1.9B (high), with a median of $837M. This wide dispersion reflects the fundamental tension between the company's early capital deployment relative to sector peers, many of which achieved substantially higher valuations at earlier stages. Key uncertainties include whether Aon3D's technology differentiation and market traction justify peer-level valuations, revenue trajectory relative to raised capital, and the timing and magnitude of next funding events. A valuation in the $50M\u2013$150M range would align with the company's funded base and stage progression, though peer multiples suggest material upside if execution and market conditions support it.",
