      "narrative": "Laminar is a Series A robotics and manufacturing company founded by Annie Lu and David Lu that has raised $12.4M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comparable universe of five private peers in robotics and manufacturing at Series A and adjacent stages, supplemented by one public comparable (ticker 277810.KQ).\n\nTwo triangulation methods were applied. The stage-progression method uses total capital raised as a valuation proxy and applies a 2.0x step-up multiplier typical of Series A to subsequent-stage progression, yielding $25M. The peer-median method benchmarks against five same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables\u2014Generalist AI ($2.0B Series B), Bedrock Robotics ($1.8B Series B), Dexterity ($1.6B Series B), Humanoid ($1.4B Series A), and Walden Robotics ($1.1B Seed)\u2014producing a median valuation of $1.6B and range of $1.1B to $2.0B.\n\nThe wide dispersion between methods reflects fundamental uncertainty regarding Laminar's position within its peer cohort. The triangulated range spans $21M to $1.9B with a median of $837M. The stage-progression floor assumes minimal market differentiation relative to capital deployed, while the peer-median reflects recent market valuations in robotics that may not yet incorporate company-specific traction or risk factors. Critical uncertainties include revenue, capital efficiency relative to peers, technological differentiation, and whether the peer set\u2014dominated by Series B+ rounds\u2014appropriately anchors a Series A company. Resolution of these factors will be essential to narrowing this range.",
