      "narrative": "Unlimited Industries is a seed-stage housing and construction company founded by Alex Modon, Jordan Stern, and Tara Viswanathan. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of five private peers in the same sector, including BotBuilt, Apis Cor, Ground Control Development, ADMARES, and Hedral. No public comparables are available, which constrains benchmarking but is typical for this nascent frontier-tech segment.\n\nThe analysis applies a stage-progression method, using the company's $12M total raised as a valuation proxy. A 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of seed-to-next-stage advancement yields an implied valuation of $30M. This represents the single applicable triangulation method given available data. The resulting range is $26M (low), $30M (median), to $34M (high), anchored to a 2.5x uplift assumption on deployment capital.\n\nKey uncertainties center on the representativeness of the private comp set and the appropriateness of the 2.5x step-up multiplier for this sector. With only one valuation method applied and no public market anchors, the range should be treated as preliminary. Refinement would require detailed financial metrics from peer financings, revenue traction from Unlimited Industries, and clarity on market-specific scaling dynamics in frontier construction technology.",
