      "narrative": "Dark, a Seed-stage space and aerospace company founded by Clyde Laheyne and Guillaume Orvain, has raised $11M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 5 public Space & Aerospace tickers (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Starcloud, SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space.\n\nOf three potential triangulation methods, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. This method applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, anchoring to the $11M total raised as a proxy baseline. This yields an implied valuation of $28M. Peer-Median comparison was inapplicable due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables in the narrow Space & Aerospace Seed cohort (only 1 same-stage peer identified; minimum of 3 required for statistical confidence). Public-Comp Anchoring could not be deployed absent disclosed revenue figures for the target; while the sector median P/S stands at 24.4x across the public set, private companies rarely disclose revenue needed for this calculation.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $23M to $32M, centered on $28M. Key uncertainties include the lack of private peer granularity and absence of revenue data, both of which would strengthen confidence. Stage progression remains the sole quantitative anchor available.",
