      "narrative": "Blumen Systems is a Seed-stage climate and energy company founded by Hannes Boehning that has raised $6.4M to date. The broader Climate & Energy sector comprises one public comparable (LNZA) and eight private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix. However, the private peer set lacks sufficient density at the Seed stage or adjacent stages with comparable valuation tiers to support a reliable peer-median methodology.\n\nConsequently, valuation relies on stage-progression analysis. Using total capital raised ($6.4M) as a proxy for current implied value and applying a typical 2.5x multiplier for advancement from Seed to the subsequent stage yields an implied valuation of $16M. This reflects the pricing step-up observed across sector participants as companies mature beyond initial funding.\n\nThe triangulation supports a valuation range of $14M to $18M, with a median of $16M. This range is derived from a single applicable method and should be treated as indicative rather than definitive. Key uncertainties include the absence of recent financing data from direct peer transactions at comparable stages, which limits calibration of the step-up multiplier. The valuation is also sensitive to assumptions about the company's operating traction and capital efficiency relative to the broader Climate & Energy cohort.",
