      "narrative": "Bountiful is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Megan Nunes, Tomas Svitek, and Michael Bertino, having raised $5.0M to date. The robotics and manufacturing sector peer set comprises 1 public company (277810.KQ) and 8 private peers including Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, Locus Robotics, and Generalist AI.\n\nA peer-median approach is not applicable here. While 11 same-sector peers exist, the narrow comparable set\u2014filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar valuation tier\u2014yielded insufficient datapoints (fewer than 3 required) to support a reliable multiple-based valuation. This reflects the challenges of establishing comps in the seed-stage robotics subsegment. Consequently, the valuation relies on stage-progression methodology, which applies a 2.5x step-up multiplier to the $5.0M total raised as a proxy for current value, implying a post-money valuation of $12.5M.\n\nThe triangulated range is $11M to $14M, with a median of $12M. This single-method result carries material uncertainty. The applicability of the 2.5x multiplier depends on Bountiful's execution trajectory relative to seed-stage peers and the timing of next-round financing. The absence of sufficient narrow comparables limits confidence in this valuation and suggests that revised analysis incorporating additional operational or product-readiness data would strengthen the estimate. Investors should treat this as a preliminary frame pending deeper diligence on technical validation and market traction.",
