      "narrative": "Ephemeris Net is a Seed-stage Space & Aerospace company founded by Dennis Fong and Nicolas Brown that has raised $3M to date. The broader sector comprises 5 public comparables (RKLB, PL, LUNR, ASTS, SATL) and 8 private peers including Starcloud, SpaceX, Rocket Lab, ICEYE, and Sierra Space, though identifying tightly matched Seed-stage peers within this universe proved limited.\n\nOf three valuation methods examined, only Stage-Progression proved applicable. Using total capital raised ($3M) as a proxy for current valuation and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the next funding round yields an implied valuation of $8M. The Peer-Median approach could not be executed due to insufficient same-stage and adjacent-stage comparables (only 1 same-stage peer identified across the broader Space & Aerospace set; 3+ required). Public-Comp Anchoring using the sector's median P/S multiple of 24.4x across five public companies was inapplicable absent the target's revenue figures, which private companies typically do not disclose.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $6M to $9M, with a median point of $8M. This range reflects sensitivity around the step-up multiplier (2.5x baseline \u00b115%) given reliance on a single method. Key uncertainties include the composition of the company's revenue model relative to public and private peers, and whether the current $3M proxy accurately reflects recent transaction activity or market signals on the company's progress.",
