      "narrative": "Valstad is a Seed-stage Defense & Security company founded by Dustin Walper that has raised $2.6M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a comp universe of 10 private and 2 public companies operating in the same sector at comparable or adjacent stages, including peers such as UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, Castelion, and Shield AI.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression, anchoring to the $2.6M total raised as a $3M proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of Seed-to-next-stage advancement, implies a $6M valuation. Peer-Median triangulation across three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables (UFORCE at $1.0B, Singularity at $400M, NODA AI at $125M) yields a median implied valuation of $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis across both methods supports a range of $6M to $460M, with a median of $203M. This wide spread reflects substantial uncertainty inherent in early-stage valuation within a sector characterized by significant dispersion in peer valuations. Stage-progression produces a more conservative estimate grounded in capital raised, while peer-median valuation is highly sensitive to the composition and stage-matching of the comparables selected. Key uncertainties include Valstad's specific technical differentiation relative to peers and the sustainability of current Defense & Security valuations.",
