      "narrative": "Determinant Materials is a seed-stage frontier-technology company in the Climate & Energy sector founded by Nikhil R. Gupta. The analysis draws from a universe of 9 peer companies (1 public, 8 private) including firms such as Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix.\n\nA single valuation method proved applicable to this analysis. Stage-progression anchored to the company's $2.5M total capital raised applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from seed to the next stage, implying a valuation of $6M. This method is appropriate given the early stage and lack of operating revenue, but peer-median analysis could not be applied due to insufficient comparable datapoints\u2014while 8 same-sector peers exist, none met criteria for tight stage, timing, or valuation-tier matching. Broadening the peer set to all Climate & Energy companies would introduce material bias.\n\nThe triangulation yields a range of $5M to $7M, with a median of $6M. This narrow range reflects methodological constraint: reliance on a single applicable approach limits the robustness of the estimate. Key uncertainties include the company's actual progress since the $2.5M raise, the timing and terms of prior rounds, and whether sufficient traction exists to support a post-seed step-up. A more confident range would require either additional operating milestones to support revenue-based methods or identification of tighter peer comparables.",
