      "narrative": "Ghost Robotics is a Seed-stage defense and security robotics company that has raised $1.85M to date. Valuation analysis triangulates across a comparable universe of 10 private and 2 public peers in the Defense & Security sector, including UFORCE, Anduril Industries, Helsing, and public-traded benchmarks DRSHF and IDEAFORGE.NS.\n\nTwo valuation methods were applied. Stage-Progression analysis uses the $1.85M raised as a proxy base value and applies a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier from Seed to next-stage financing, implying a $5M valuation. Peer-Median analysis examines three same-sector, same/adjacent-stage comparables: UFORCE (Seed, $1.0B), Singularity (Series A, $400M), and NODA AI (Series A, $125M). The median of this peer set is $400M, with a range spanning $125M to $1.0B.\n\nThe triangulated analysis produces a wide implied range: low of $4M, median of $202M, and high of $460M. The substantial spread reflects the extreme variance in peer valuations and the tension between capital-efficiency metrics (Stage-Progression) and sector-specific scaling multiples (Peer-Median). Key uncertainties include the maturity and revenue traction of peer companies, market timing of Ghost Robotics' next funding round, and whether defense-sector valuation multiples have normalized since the sample period. The Stage-Progression floor of $4M represents a floor consistent with capital invested; the peer median implies significant optionality pricing.",
