      "narrative": "Voltra is a seed-stage climate & energy company founded by Alexander Stratmoen and Aryan Afrouzi that has raised $1.8M to date. The frontier-tech climate sector comprises a fragmented peer set of 1 public company (Lianza, ticker LNZA) and 8 private peers including Redwood Materials, QuantumScape, KoBold Metals, Electric Hydrogen, and Enovix, though none provide reliable same-stage or adjacent-stage comparables.\n\nPeer-median valuation was not applicable due to insufficient datapoints meeting narrow stage and valuation-tier filters within the climate & energy sector. Accordingly, stage-progression analysis was the primary method employed. Using $1.8M total raised as a proxy for seed-stage base value and applying a typical 2.5x step-up multiplier to the subsequent round, this method implies a valuation of $4.5M. This reflects observed progression patterns from seed to early Series A in frontier energy and materials technology.\n\nThe analysis supports a valuation range of $3.8M to $5.2M, with a median point of $4M\u2013$4.5M. Key uncertainties include the absence of direct peer comparables at equivalent stages, which limits confidence in the step-up multiplier applied, and the nascent, heterogeneous nature of the frontier climate sector itself. Additional fundraising activity or technical milestones would warrant reassessment.",
