      "narrative": "Fid Labs is a seed-stage robotics and manufacturing company founded by Adam Wolnikowski that has raised $1.7M to date. The valuation analysis draws from a broader comp universe of 9 private and 1 public robotics companies, including peers like Walden Robotics, Divergent, Exotec, and Locus Robotics.\n\nStage-progression methodology is the primary applicable approach here. Using the $1.7M in total raised as a valuation proxy and applying a 2.5x multiplier typical of seed-to-Series A step-ups yields an implied valuation of $4.25M. This method is appropriate given the company's seed stage and the absence of sufficient narrow peer comparables. Peer-median analysis could not be reliably applied: while 11 robotics companies exist in the broader comp set, filtering for same-stage, adjacent-stage, and similar valuation-tier peers yielded fewer than the three minimum datapoints needed for statistical confidence. An all-sector median would risk introducing material bias given the heterogeneity of robotics company profiles.\n\nThe triangulated valuation range of $4M to $5M (median $4.25M) is supported by a single method. Key uncertainties include the absence of robust peer comps at Fid Labs' specific stage and tier, limiting cross-validation of the stage-progression result. Further valuation confidence would benefit from closer comparables or additional founder/product-specific data clarifying competitive positioning within the robotics manufacturing subsector.",
